{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'implementation_notes|RVFI port set' .gitignore CLAUDE.md && cat cores/bench/rtl/{hazard_unit,id_stage,mem_stage}.sv && ls -la formal && ls -la bench/programs\"", "aggregated_output": "CLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:58:`cores/<TARGET>/test/test_*.py`. The agent's `implementation_notes.md`\nCLAUDE.md:59:lives at `cores/<TARGET>/implementation_notes.md` (gitignored). The\nCLAUDE.md:81:- Change `core`'s top-level IO shape relative to the `nret` value declared in `core.yaml` — specifically: the imem/dmem port set, and the RVFI port set (only `_0` fields for `nret: 1`; both `_0` and `_1` for `nret: 2` with channel-0-older convention and the single-retire-on-channel-0 rule).\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\n// rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n//\n// Detects the only data hazard the textbook 5-stage doesn't cover via\n// forwarding: load-use. A LOAD in EX produces its data only after MEM,\n// so an instruction immediately behind that consumes the LOAD's rd\n// must be stalled by exactly one cycle.\n//\n// IF and ID share a cycle. On a load-use hazard IF retries the same PC\n// and ID inserts a bubble. An EX correction squashes the single younger\n// slot. Holds for memory or divide take priority at ID/EX.\n//\n// Latency:        combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    n/a (