{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"tail -60 cores/bench/LESSONS.md; nproc; cat /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max; cat /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max; printenv | rg '\"'^(JOBS|CORE_NAME|RTL_DIR|PATH|PYTHONPATH|VIRTUAL_ENV|GOWIN_HOME)='\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +471.29%): Folding combinational DIV/REM into four steps of eight quotient bits shortened the EX critical path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 31.097 MHz, while timed cycles stayed flat because CoreMark executes all five DIVU sites outside its timing markers.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +9.82%): Predicting the next PC from decode operands and flushing only when EX resolved a different successor saved a fetch slot on correctly predicted taken transfers, cutting the prototype's timed CoreMark cycles by 7.3%.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r2s0 (regression, +37.09%): Cutting the `remainder_q` feedback chain from eight to five trial subtractions per clock raised median Gowin Fmax to 43.681 MHz and moved the critical path to the ID/EX operand registers, while the three extra rounds per divide cost no timed cycles because CoreMark executes no DIV/REM between markers.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r2s1 (improvement, +43.23%): Registering 3D in a setup cycle let each radix-4 digit test D, 2D and 3D in parallel, raising Fmax by cutting the divider's remainder feedback path from eight dependent subtract/select stages to three.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.63%): Reusing taken targets in a 128-entry fetch-PC BTB saved 301,480 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, a 6.7% reduction too small to offset the radix-4 divider's clock advantage (45.64 vs 32.885 MHz).\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r3s0 (regression, +8.66%): Registering the forwarded `rs1 + imm` sum at EX/MEM kept the multiplier DSP and EX result mux off the `dmem_addr` path, raising median Gowin Fmax from 45.640 to 49.590 MHz with the same timed CoreMark cycle count.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r3s1 (regression, +11.24%): A one-entry fall-through buffer let decode issue a word saved during a load-use or data-memory stall even with `imem_ready` low, cutting timed CoreMark cycles by 3.1% versus 6.4% for direct-branch prediction at a similar Fmax.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261\n…[8314 of 11386 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:87b11e35a5c301c5]…\n, leaving the path from `saved_value` through subword verification to the load-table write port limiting median Fmax to 85.978 MHz against the 87.29 MHz replacement threshold.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-003-r12s2 (regression, -1.52%): Rotating each load-predictor row to the last byte offset saved 218 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but forwarding `saved_word` through the next load’s index adder, table read and sign extension to `predicted_value` cut median Fmax from 83.455 to 82.178 MHz.\n20\ncat: /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max: No such file or directory\ncat: /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max: No such file or directory\nGOWIN_HOME=/opt/gowin\nPATH=/srv/hwebench/cli/codex-0.170.0/codex-pkg/codex-path:/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/.codex-home/tmp/arg0-linux/codex-arg0FjPLFs:/srv/hwebench/cli/codex-0.170.0:/srv/hwebench/bin:/srv/hwebench/venv/bin:/srv/hwebench/local/bin:/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin:/srv/hwebench/toolchain/bin:/srv/hwebench/venv/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'ls -la formal; cat tools/eval/gowin.py; cat tools/eval/cosim.py; ls -la bench/programs'", "aggregated_output": "total 56\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 23 08:55 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 23 08:56 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 23 08:55 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 23 08:55 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 23 08:55 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+  1 nobody nogroup    68 Nov 23 08:55 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+  1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 23 08:55 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  4615 Nov 23 08:55 wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2863 Nov 23 08:55 wrapper_si.sv\n\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=T\n…[16948 of 20020 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0319fbc33558935a]…\nlf'],\n                'detail': cm_result,\n            }\n\n    tested = len(trace_elfs) + (1 if coremark else 0)\n    return {'passed': True, 'elfs_tested': tested}\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    result = run_cosim(\n        sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else '.',\n        sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else None,\n    )\n    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\ntotal 464\ndrwxrwx---+  3 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 23 08:55 .\ndrwxrwx---+  3 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 23 08:55 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   2317 Nov 23 08:55 Makefile\ndrwxrwx---+ 14 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 23 08:55 coremark\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup    135 Nov 23 08:55 crt0.S\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   6341 Nov 23 08:55 gen_random_trace.py\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup    330 Nov 23 08:55 link.ld\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 140494 Nov 23 08:55 random1.S\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 138125 Nov 23 08:55 random2.S\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 142438 Nov 23 08:55 random3.S\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   3684 Nov 23 08:55 selftest.S\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
