{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_108","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; cmp cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv \"$TMPDIR/mem-distributed.sv\"; git status --short --untracked-files=normal; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; date -u'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Registered load-table writes\n\nMEM captures the true index, tag, format signature and raw word at the MEM/WB edge. A one-cycle install strobe drives the following RAM write. The write port and its collision bypass share the same 64-bit row, including the 17-bit narrow value formed from the registered signature and word.\n\nOccupancy changes on logical acceptance. This lets a narrow store invalidate its row immediately using the existing occupancy bit, with no physical write. A simultaneous logical update rejects the lookup even if an older install is committing to the same index. A bus stall holds the captured candidate and speculative value while the pending install drains. Reset clears occupancy and the strobe and suppresses the write.\n\nThe directed pipeline test alternates tags at one index, stalls the third request for three clocks, reads during both a signed halfword fill and an unsigned byte refresh, and checks a narrow-store invalidation. It checks the one-cycle install strobe during the stall, accepted bus accesses, RVFI raw words, dependent values and retirement gaps.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings.\n- All six cocotb test modules passed, including the pipeline suite. Fast ALTOPS formal passed all 53 checks on the first attempt.\n- Selftest cosimulation passed with both ready signals high and with randomized stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRC checks and reported correct operation.\n- Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,140,795 cycles between markers 11,974 and 3,152,769.\n\n## Timing\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 81.518, 81.731 and 81.731 MHz. The 81.731 MHz median falls below the 92.80 MHz replacement target and gives 260.22 iterations/s. Placement 0 now ends at the speculative load-value register after a WB-to-EX lookup. The other placements are limited by a path from the saved raw word through load verification to the divider remainder register.\nMon Nov 23 09:40:16 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
