{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_158","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'SLICE|Logic|Register|SSRAM|BSRAM' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/pnr-h/impl/pnr/core_bench.rpt.txt\" | head -15; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"43:  Logic                       | 4472/20736                          |  22%\n45:    --SSRAM(RAM16)            | 56                                  | -\n46:  Register                    | 1293/15750                          |  9%\n47:    --Logic Register as Latch | 0/15552                             |  0%\n48:    --Logic Register as FF    | 1293/15552                          |  9%\n49:    --I/O Register as Latch   | 0/198                               |  0%\n50:    --I/O Register as FF      | 0/198                               |  0%\n57:  BSRAM                       | 8/46                                | 18%\n# EX/MEM result split\n\nID registers the validated ALU selects with the instruction. EX adds the two forwarded registers in parallel with the effective-address calculation. ADD selects the register sum and ADDI selects the effective address. Their masked OR feeds a dedicated 32-bit register. A second register captures the enabled non-add results, including the link address and a divide result on response transfer. The OR of the two registers feeds MEM and EX forwarding.\n\nBoth result registers sample on every clock. A stalled store uses its held address and data. A stalled load gets its value from the load bypass or WB. Pipeline validity and the registered producer controls suppress writes from bubbles and traps.\n\nThe ALU unit tests exercise the split outputs directly, including a negative ADDI with a different value on the rs2 input.\n\n## Local verification\n\nThe initial split passed lint, all six cocotb suites, and co-simulation for selftest, three random programs and CoreMark. Ten iterations took 3,207,017 bracketed cycles with all five expected CRCs. Timing refinement and formal verification are in progress.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
