he prior Chisel iteration. Each must be\nenforced by a check that fails loudly when violated. **Do not weaken these\nchecks** to make a hypothesis pass.\n\n## Hard invariants\n\n| # | Invariant                                                                                                  | Enforced by                                  |\n|---|-----\n…[7121 of 10193 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:acb0d8fdbe7fb754]…\n7)\n333:async def load_div_rem_store_with_stalls(dut):\n336:        LW(1, 0, 0),       # -101, forwarded from WB to the first divide\n340:        SW(5, 0, 4),       # consume the immediately preceding divide\n350:        # the last divide's transfer. Stall each data access for three edges.\n383:    would let a wrong-path retirement with rd=0 / trap=1 / different data\n392:    # Strict: no retirement should originate from PC=4.\n394:    assert not leaked, f\"wrong-path retirement leaked from PC=4: {leaked}\"\n395:    # Strict: no retirement carries the skipped instruction word at all.\n400:    assert pcs == [0, 8, 12], f\"unexpected retirement PC sequence: {pcs}\"\n408:    # The exit decrements a strongly-taken counter to weakly taken.\n759:async def subword_branch_and_divide_replay(dut):\n864:    # bus word is 7, so only a premature branch resolution would skip SW.\n1030:    assert pcs == [0, 8, 12], f\"unexpected retirement PC sequence: {pcs}\"\n1050:    assert pcs == [0, 4, 12, 16], f\"unexpected retirement PC sequence: {pcs}\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
