{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_151","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --stat'","aggregated_output":"# Shared RV32 divider\n\nOne radix-16 array handles DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. Its 15 trials subtract 20-bit operands with separate borrow bits and feed back a 16-bit residual. Even-multiple comparisons select a pair of candidates while the odd-multiple comparison selects the residual within each pair. A dedicated divisor register drives the power-of-two trial inputs. Only the setup logic for the odd multiples uses the phase-selected operand.\n\nSmall nonzero divisors use the prefix lookup and seven trials. Large divisors use fixed shifts of 1, 2, 4, 8 or 16 bits, four quotient digits, and a registered unsigned 16-by-16 product of the estimate and discarded divisor bits. The response subtraction produces the residual and borrow for a single correction. A zero divisor returns an all-ones quotient and the original dividend as remainder.\n\nThe sequencer starts on a verified request handshake. The response becomes valid seven clocks later and holds until accepted. EX/MEM registers the quotient, residual, borrow, signed correction term and operation flags independently of the integer bypass. MEM combines sign restoration and correction in one addition with carry-in.\n\nI also moved the load/execute result selection before MEM/WB after the first placement identified the WB mux on its longest path. Forwarding, register-file writes and RVFI now use one registered result. The existing WB interlock still controls divide consumers.\n\nDirected ALU cases cover both neighbors of each scale threshold, maximal low-part products, both correction outcomes, signed operand combinations, overflow, division by zero and held responses. The pipeline test checks a corrected negative quotient and remainder through retirement and their immediate ALU and store consumers.\n cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv            | 217 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           |   4 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  22 +++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  25 +++--\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      |  16 +--\n cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv       |   9 +-\n cores/bench/test/test_alu.py      |  61 +++++++++--\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py |  24 +++++\n 8 files changed, 265 insertions(+), 113 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
