 need 15. These bounds\\ncover both kD and every eligible partial dividend. The largest class\\nconsumes successive prefixes of a 32-bit dividend. Use a separate borrow\\nbit and mark ineligible trials as losing before selecting the largest\\nfitting digit. A digit wins when it fits and its successor does not,\\nwith digit zero always fitting. Register the winning\n…[7454 of 10526 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8d1e469ed2ec7c22]…\n\\n3,140,795 cycles the replacement threshold requires about 87.3 MHz.\\nMeasure the cycle cost of changing row orientation together with median\\nGowin Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the tagged rotated word and offset, derive both the predicted operand and MEM raw word from it, and refresh on a verified word with a mismatched lane.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the producer's load width and signedness alongside the existing speculative row index so MEM can register its fixed-slice bypass candidate.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise all four byte orientations, alternating signedness, halfword and word promotion, a same-row collision, and a dependent branch during an external stall. Check load masks, raw words, register results and retirement PCs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"d\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
