{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_129","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --check; git status --short --ignored | head -18'","aggregated_output":"# Four quotient bits per clock in MEM\n\nThe local Gowin median was **70.061 MHz**. Ten validated CoreMark iterations took **3,207,017 marker cycles** with both stall generators active, yielding **218.46 iterations/s**. This is 6.09% above the 205.93 iterations/s baseline and clears the 4.6% cutoff.\n\n| Gowin placement | Fmax (MHz) | Logic cells |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 64.479 | 4,438 |\n| 1 | 70.061 | 4,438 |\n| 2 | 70.061 | 4,438 |\n\n## Implementation\n\nEX issues DIV/REM and captures its forwarded RVFI operands in EX/MEM on the same edge. Dedicated divider inputs bypass the PC and immediate operand muxes. The accepted request marks the MEM slot as occupied until its response transfers to MEM/WB. An independent divide can issue on that transfer edge. All eight M operations use the existing WB dependency interlock.\n\nThe 32-bit quotient register holds the dividend magnitude at issue. Setup reads the 256-by-8 prefix ROM for divisors below 16 and registers the first quotient nibble, the residual, and 3D. Seven rounds each consume two radix-4 digits using parallel trials against D, 2D, and 3D. Signed result restoration feeds MEM/WB directly. The real divider and ALTOPS share the eight-clock response schedule.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with the requested warning flags.\n- All 104 cocotb cases passed. Directed tests covered every prefix ROM entry, the wide-divisor bypass, signed corner cases, response backpressure, and reset during turnover. Independent divides retired nine clocks apart. The dependent divide retired ten clocks after its producer, and its operands and stored result matched RVFI.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the reference ISS on ready buses and with both stall generators active. CoreMark reported all five expected CRCs and validated its ten iterations.\n\nPlacement remains the main timing sensitivity. The limiting path ends at the fetch successor table's occupancy bits. It starts in the register file for placement 0 and in the MEM word table for placements 1 and 2.\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
