{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"env | rg '\"'^(CORE_NAME|RTL_DIR|NRET|JOBS|GOWIN_[A-Za-z_]+)='\"'; ls -l /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh; cat formal/checks_si.cfg; ls -la /srv/hwebench/toolchain/bin\"", "aggregated_output": "GOWIN_HOME=/opt/gowin\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 nobody nogroup 24968 Jul 10  2025 /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\ntotal 148\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 ..\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   81 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-addr2line -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-addr2line\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   74 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-ar -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-ar\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   74 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-as -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpa\n…[4025 of 7097 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3437e4920c386a66]…\nlf-objcopy -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-objcopy\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   79 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-objdump -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-objdump\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   78 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-ranlib -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-ranlib\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   79 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-readelf -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-readelf\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   76 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-size -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-size\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   79 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-strings -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-strings\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup   77 Sep 28 02:44 riscv32-unknown-elf-strip -> /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1/bin/riscv-none-elf-strip\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
