{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_157","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'Target|logic [0-9]|MHz' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/predictor-single-row-all.log\"; rg -n '\"'Time|elapsed|warning|WARN' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/correction_match/gw.log\" | tail -8; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; date -u'","aggregated_output":"49:WARN  (EX3780) : Using initial value of 'i' since it is never assigned(\"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-003-r10s2/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\":72)\n50:WARN  (EX3780) : Using initial value of 'i' since it is never assigned(\"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261123-003-r10s2/cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\":73)\n# Split direction predictor\n\nFetch uses PC[10:2] for 512 direction bits and PC[8:2] for 128 shared strength bits. Both tables initialize to zero, giving weak fallthrough. The instruction carries its sampled direction, strength, and selected successor through ID/EX. An advancing decoded conditional branch registers those inputs and its index at the EX edge. One cycle later, the selected-taken bit XOR correction_q gives the aligned outcome. A direction match sets strength. A weak sample takes the outcome as its new direction.\n\nThe direction RAM packs the four directions that share a strength into one four-bit word. The pipeline carries that word alongside the branch and forwards older writes to it through holds. This preserves the other three directions on a word write. The fetch bypass compares all nine index bits for direction and seven for strength.\n\nDirected tests cover both index widths, independent forwarding, forced fallthrough, retirement PCs and wrong-path stores. The load-replay test counts committed predictor writes on release.\n\nStrict Verilator lint passed. Selftest and three randomized programs passed RVFI cosimulation with and without bus stalls. Ten CoreMark iterations with both stalls took 3,126,803 bracketed cycles, saving 13,992 cycles. All five CRCs matched and UART reported correct operation.\n\nThe initial scalar RAM implementation passed all 53 local formal checks. Formal verification and the full three-option timing measurement for the packed implementation are in progress.\nMon Nov 23 05:05:24 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
