{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_128", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 2 \"$TMPDIR\"/rotate/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p?/gw.log; tail -n 3 \"$TMPDIR/rotate/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-canonical/checks/reg_ch0/logfile.txt\"; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; date -u'", "aggregated_output": "==> /srv/hwebench/tmp/51daa901/4c006217/rotate/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p0/gw.log <==\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\n\n==> /srv/hwebench/tmp/51daa901/4c006217/rotate/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p1/gw.log <==\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\n\n==> /srv/hwebench/tmp/51daa901/4c006217/rotate/cores/bench/generated/gowin_p2/gw.log <==\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\nSBY  8:12:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:08  Checking assertions in step 20..\nSBY  8:13:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:08  waiting for solver (1 minute)\nSBY  8:17:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:05:08  waiting for solver (5 minutes)\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Rotated load-predictor rows\n\nEach of the 256 rows holds a 10-bit SRAM tag, a two-bit byte offset and one 32-bit rotated word. This saves 5,120 table bits. The issuing load's width and signedness select a registered operand from fixed slices. MEM releases the dependent instruction after checking the word address, occupancy, alignment, collision status and byte offset.\n\nA resident load at a new offset retires internally and refreshes the row even while the bus is stalled. Its adjacent consumer replays once using WB. Internal completions inverse-rotate the word for RVFI. Accepted aligned SW installs offset zero and accepted narrow SRAM stores invalidate the indexed row.\n\nThe implementation combines the inverse rotation and the new fill rotation into one rotate by the difference between offsets. The row and its formatted candidate hold together during an external stall.\n\n## CoreMark\n\nTen CRC-validated iterations with both stall generators enabled took 3,140,577 cycles between the MMIO markers. The champion rerun took 3,140,795 cycles, a saving of 218 cycles (0.0069%). The optional Verilator `+load_profile` counter observed 65,685 bypass hits in 83,975 adjacent subword uses. Offset changes on verified words caused 14,976 adjacent subword replays and zero adjacent LW replays.\n\n| Gowin metric | Champion | Rotated rows |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Placement 0 (MHz) | 77.594 | 80.311 |\n| Placement 1 (MHz) | 83.455 | 82.178 |\n| Placement 2 (MHz) | 83.455 | 82.178 |\n| Median (MHz) | 83.455 | 82.178 |\n| CoreMark iterations/s | 265.71 | 261.67 |\n| Logic cells | 7,349 | 6,728 |\n| Registers | 1,462 | 1,434 |\n| LUT-RAM cells | 312 | 232 |\n\nThe smaller table missed the roughly 87.3 MHz replacement threshold. In the median placements the longest path runs from bit 2 of the saved word through EX operand forwarding, the partial index adder and the next table read to bit 20 of the next registered prediction. The divider sets the limit in placement 0. The single table and fully registered formatted operand gave the highest measured median among the variants tried.\n\n## Directed tests\n\nThe pipeline tests check all four orientations, signed and unsigned loads at a shared offset, promotion to halfword and word, same-row collisions, narrow-store invalidation, MMIO aliases and dependent branches across bus stalls. They check retirement order and PCs, operand values, load masks, canonical RVFI words and the cycle gap from load to consumer.\n\n## Local verification\n\nVerilator lint passed with all requested warnings enabled. All six cocotb suites passed. The single-retirement formal gate passed all 53 checks on the first run. Cosim passed selftest and three random instruction traces with and without stalls, and passed stalled CoreMark with all five expected CRCs and the validation banner.\nMon Nov 23 07:18:26 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
