{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cmp cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv \"$TMPDIR/verify/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-pairs/mem_stage.sv\" && git diff --check && git status --short && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Load-value predictor write port\n\nMEM captures an eight-bit index, a packed 64-bit row, and the update and install enables. On the next edge the port installs the row and sets occupancy together, or clears occupancy for a narrow store. The port drains during bus holds and accepts consecutive updates. Reset clears occupancy and cancels queued work.\n\nAn advancing lookup records collisions with the incoming update and the committing packet. The candidate and its collision information hold together across stalls. Subword verification compares each pair of bits in parallel so each equality fits in a four-input LUT. The predictor still checks the entire byte, the extension, the signature and the full word address.\n\nDirected tests cover consecutive stores, a commit colliding with a lookup of a resident row, a commit during a bus stall, a younger byte-store invalidation, and reset with a replacement pending. The existing format-refresh tests allow the initial fill to commit before they probe its signature.\n\n## Local results\n\n- Verilator lint and all 114 cocotb cases passed. Cosimulation passed for five ELFs, including the stalled CoreMark run with all five expected CRCs and the validation message.\n- The CoreMark markers occurred at cycles 11,974 and 3,152,769. Ten iterations took 3,140,795 cycles, matching the baseline.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 74.333, 86.164 and 86.164 MHz. The median gives 274.34 iterations/s against 282.47 at the 88.718 MHz baseline. Throughput fell 2.88%, missing the 92.80 MHz replacement threshold.\n- On both median placements the longest path runs from the instruction successor RAM to the predicted PC register. Moving the load predictor write port removed it from the reported worst path.\n- The single-channel ALTOPS formal suite passed all 53 checks on the final RTL, including register consistency. It produced no counterexample and required no fix attempt.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
