{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv; rg -n 'pc|valid|stall|predicted' cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv; cat ../../LESSONS.md\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/ex_stage.sv\n//\n// Execute stage. Resolves the operand muxes (forwarding from EX/MEM and\n// MEM/WB), runs the ALU, resolves branches, computes the redirect\n// target. Owns the EX/MEM pipeline register.\n//\n// A load consumer uses the synchronous table output while MEM verifies\n// its address and format. A failed verification kills this execution at the edge.\n//\n// Latency:        1 cycle for fast ops. DIV/REM hold ID/EX until completion.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_wdata (= pc_next), the rd_wdata path for\n//                 ALU and JAL/JALR (PC+4), and the branch resolve.\nmodule ex_stage (\n  input  logic               clock,\n  input  logic               reset,\n  input  logic               stall,         // freeze EX/MEM register (dmem stall)\n  input  logic               replay,        // keep ID/EX and bubble EX/MEM on release\n  input  id_ex_t   in,\n  input  bypass_t            fwd_rs1_sel,\n  input  bypass_t            fwd_rs2_sel,\n  input  bypass_t            alu_b_sel,\n  input  logic [31:0]        predicted_value,\n  input  logic               rs1_trace_load,\n  input  logic               rs2_trace_load,\n  input  logic [31:0]        fwd_ex_mem,    // EX/MEM.alu_result (registered)\n  input  logic [31:0]        fwd_mem_wb,    // WB-stage write-data mux output\n  output ex_mem_t  out,\n  output logic [7:0]         lookup_index,\n  output logic               div_wait,\n  output logic               will_write,\n  output logic               redirect,\n  output logic [31:0]        redirect_target,\n  output logic               fence_i,\n  output logic               train_en,\n  output logic [6:0]         train_index,\n  output logic [1:0]         train_counter\n);\n\n  // ── Operand forwarding muxes ───────────────────────────────────────────\n  logic [31:0] rs1;\n  logic [31:0] rs2;\n\n  function automatic logic [31:0] operand(input bypass_t sel, input logic [31:0] captured);\n    operand = ({32{sel.captured}} & captured)\n            | ({32{sel.mem_wb}}   & fwd_mem_wb)\n            | ({32{sel.ex_mem}}   & fwd_ex_mem)\n            | (\n…[18571 of 21643 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:125755a883ae5666]…\n 86.62 MHz needed for replacement.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-001-r14s0 (regression, -7.88%): Registering load-table fills preserved CoreMark’s 3,140,795 timed cycles, but the WB lookup feeding `predicted_value` limited placement 0 and load verification from `saved_raw` to the divider’s `remainder_q` limited the other two placements, cutting median Fmax from 88.718 to 81.731 MHz.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-002-r14s1 (regression, -9.88%): Forwarding a buffered load-table update on a same-row lookup preserved CoreMark’s 3,140,795 timed cycles, but selecting occupancy for that row made the path from WB’s `mem_to_reg` through the EX lookup index to `candidate_valid` critical, cutting median Fmax from 88.718 to 79.955 MHz.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-003-r14s2 (regression, -2.88%): Rejecting same-row load-predictor lookups at both update capture and commit preserved CoreMark’s 3,140,795 timed cycles, but the path from the fetch successor RAM to `predicted_pc_q` limited median Fmax to 86.164 MHz, down from 88.718 MHz.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
