{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_194","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --numstat; date -u'","aggregated_output":"# Four-entry return-address stack\n\nThe core predicts the exact `jalr x0,0(x1)` encoding from live instructions and verified successor records. Fetch registers the chosen stack word alongside the ordinary PC calculation. ID/EX retains its own copy with the instruction during stalls and replay. EX compares the saved target against bits [31:1] of each rs1 bypass candidate in parallel. A wrong aligned target redirects to forwarded x1 with bit zero cleared. A set bit one traps and recovers to PC+4.\n\nEach advancing aligned call to x1 pushes its architectural PC+4. An out-of-RAM link occupies an invalid slot. Each advancing aligned return pops, including a return issued without a prediction. Reset and an advancing FENCE.I clear validity.\n\nTwo timing refinements affect the implementation. The four validity bits shift on the advancing EX edge. The address flops shift one edge later using registered push and pop signals. A bypass exposes the new logical top immediately and keeps the late replay decision off the address flops. EX/MEM captures the link or AUIPC result in parallel with the integer ALU result and merges them after the edge for forwarding.\n\nThe ten-iteration CoreMark run with both buses stalled took 3,128,081 marker cycles, saving 12,714 cycles (0.405%). Cosimulation passed for selftest with and without stalls. All five CoreMark CRCs matched, UART reported successful validation, and the simulation reported no out-of-bounds access.\n\nVerilator lint and all six cocotb suites passed. Directed pipeline tests cover nested calls, overflow and underflow, an out-of-range link, FENCE.I, simultaneous issue and stack update, aligned target rewrites, odd x1, bit-one traps, held calls, and load-hit and replayed returns. The tests check fetch addresses, retirement order, next PCs, and wrong-path stores.\n\nFinal RTL formal and three-placement Gowin timing runs are in progress.\n8\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n5\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n31\t8\tcores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n2\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n42\t5\tcores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n203\t0\tcores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nMon Nov 23 10:49:12 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
