{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r4s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-003-r4s2\ntitle: Predict the successor instruction from the preceding fetch PC\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion predicts direct branch targets accurately enough to save\n  289,213 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations. Even after a correct taken\n  prediction, fetching the target instruction can still cost a cycle when\n  imemReady is low. A recurring sequence of instructions provides an\n  opportunity to predict both the address and the word that will be needed.\n\n  A scratch RTL prototype on the champion reduced the ten-iteration timing\n  bracket from 4,202,272 to 3,454,614 cycles with both bus stalls active.\n  It issued 584,644 instructions from validated predictions while imemReady\n  was low, including 68,207 at nonsequential successors. All five CRCs\n  matched. Gowin placements reached 44.829, 46.629 and 46.629 MHz. The\n  median gives 134.98 iterations/s, 13.35% above 119.08.\n  At this cycle count, a median above 43.030 MHz clears the 4.6% margin.\n  The prototype passed 53 ALTOPS formal checks and 18 pipeline test cases.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give each accepted fetch one prediction of its successor instruction.\n  Read a 256-entry synchronous RAM indexed by the source PC[9:2]. Each\n  row holds the last observed successor's 18-bit word address and 32-bit\n  instruction. This read starts in parallel with the existing branch\n  direction lookup and target calculation. Keep the registered fetch PC\n  as the external imem address and as the authority for validating the guess.\n\n  On the next cycle, select live bus data whenever imemReady is high.\n  Otherwise issue the saved word only if the candidate is valid and\n  {12'b0, saved_word_address, 2'b00} equals the entire current fetch PC.\n  Source-index aliases are safe because the stored word was fetched at\n  that exact successor address. A wrong guess with an unready bus holds\n  the PC for a real response.\n  Feed the selected word to decode, load-use detection and direct-branch\n  prediction. Use bus-ready OR validated-hit as fetch availability.\n\n  Ret\n…[1057 of 4129 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3f33aaa965cf716c]…\n Implement the 256-by-50 successor RAM with one clocked read and one write, separate occupancy bits, and full-PC validation. Capture, train and advance only on accepted fetches. Prioritize live bus data in the instruction mux.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Feed IF's combined word availability to the hazard interlock, and route the advancing FENCE.I pulse from EX to IF. Keep the external imem handshake on the live bus path.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Recognize a valid advancing FENCE.I, invalidate successor predictions, and use the existing squash and redirect to restart at PC+4. Keep architectural next-PC and link calculations intact.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Withhold imem and drive a store encoding on its data pins during warm loop backedges. Check consecutive retirements, loop exit, wrong-row alias rejection and held corrections. Modify a trained instruction with a stalled store followed by FENCE.I and verify that only the new word retires on the next visit.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
