{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '85\\\\.48|272\\\\.17|critical path|median' .tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261123-001-r12s0.log | tail -15 | cut -c1-900\"", "aggregated_output": "23:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'cat tools/eval/gowin.py'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\\n\\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\\n\\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\\nimport os\\nimport re\\nimport shutil\\nimport statistics\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remo\n29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c \\\"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg -n 'invariant|RVFI' CLAUDE.md | head -14\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +471.29%): Folding combinational DIV/REM into four steps of eight quotient bits shortened the EX critical path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 31.097 MHz, while timed cycles stayed flat because CoreMark executes all five DIVU sites outside its timing markers.\\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +9.82%): Predicting the next PC from decode operands and flushing only when EX resolved a different successor saved a fetch slot on correctly predicted taken transfers, cutting the prototype's timed CoreMark cycles by 7.3%.\\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r2s0 (regression, +37.09%): Cutting the `remainder_q` feedback chain from eig\n86:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options > \\\"$TMPDIR/div-timing.log\\\" 2>&1; result=$?; tail -45 \\\"$TMPDIR/div-\n…[5433 of 8505 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5a55ca4288988adf]…\n\\\"],r[\\\\\\\"critical_paths\\\\\\\"][0]) for p in range(3)]); print(85.484e7/3140795)'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"[(0, 81.356, 7082, 1524, {'from': 'cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/predicted_pc_q_30_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.292, 'arrival_ns': 17.586, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']}), (1, 85.484, 7082, 1524, {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_24_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.698, 'arrival_ns': 16.\n409:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_206\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Implemented the four-class divider with 290 trial data bits and grouped EX/MEM residual registers. Lint, all 53 formal checks, 26 ALU tests, 37 pipeline tests, and cosimulation passed.\\n\\nCoreMark validated in **3,140,795 marker cycles**. Median Gowin Fmax was **85.484 MHz**, yielding **272.17 iterations/s** and falling short of the 87.29 MHz replacement gate.\\n\\n[Implementation notes](./cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\"}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
