{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r14s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261123-001-r14s0\ntitle: Register load-table fills before driving the RAM write port\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,140,795 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its\n  reported Gowin placement-0 path runs from effective_addr[14] to the\n  load-table RAM write port in nine cells. The current MEM stage verifies\n  the address, selects a cached or external word, extracts a signed lane\n  and drives a 256-row RAM in the same clock. Several earlier placements\n  also ended at this write port. At the champion's cycle count the median\n  must exceed 92.80 MHz to clear the replacement threshold.\nhypothesis: |\n  Pipeline the existing table write by one clock. At the MEM/WB edge\n  capture the accepted update's true index, tag, format signature, raw\n  word and install/invalidate controls. Use the registered word and\n  signature to form the 17-bit formatted field at writeback. The physical\n  RAM write address, enable and input then come from the pending update,\n  so tag verification and the external memory read finish at a register\n  before the lane formatter and RAM write port.\n\n  Preserve the present lookup timing by distinguishing the two collisions.\n  A lookup coincident with a new logical update to its index is rejected\n  exactly as today. A lookup coincident only with the physical commit of\n  an older install uses that pending row, including its tag and signature.\n  A narrow-store invalidation supplies an invalid entry. The newest logical\n  update takes priority if both match. Keep occupancy synchronized with\n  logical updates and hold the captured candidate during a data-bus stall.\n  Drain a pending update exactly once even if the next request stalls, and\n  discard pending state on reset. This permits one update per cycle and\n  predicts the champion's marker count with a shorter MEM write path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Register accepted load fills, signature refreshes and store updates. Format the pending word for RAM commit and resolve both collision ages consistently for validity, raw data and speculative forwarding.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise two successive updates to one index, a lookup at the delayed write, a narrow-store invalidation and a held request. Check bus reads, dependent results and RVFI raw words.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
