 12 cells, cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_3_s0 -> cpu/u_mem/predicted_value_22_s0\n  path 3: 17.529 ns, 11 cells, cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_8_s0 -> cpu/u_mem/predicted_value_24_s0\n  path 4: 17.523 ns, 38 cells, cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_1_s0 -> cpu/u_if/uncorrected_q_s0\n  path 5: 17.521 ns, 11 cells, cpu/u_fwd_rs1/sel.load_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_17_s0\nscore Fmax (median): 81.731 MHz\nThe pipeline regression passes, including the stalled collision and signed-halfword forwarding cases. CoreMark also passes its CRC checks and takes exactly 3,140,795 cycles between markers. Formal and Gowin timing are still running.\n72:  1     clock        200.000(MHz)   81.731(MHz)   13      TOP     \n  1     clock        200.000(MHz)   81.731(MHz)   13      TOP     \n  1     clock        200.000(MHz)   81.731(MHz)   13      TOP     \nThe first implementation passed all 53 formal checks, but its median was 81.731 MHz. Gowin shows the critical path has moved away from the RAM write port. I’ll check whether the existing split-address lookup can verify its index earlier while preserving the same hit decisions.\nI retained the single distributed-RAM table. The alternative layouts and bypasses I measured had lower median Fmax. The retained RTL passed formal, the full unit suite, and cosimulation, but it falls short of the replacement threshold.\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 81.518, 81.731 and 81.731 MHz. The 81.731 MHz median falls below the 92.80 MHz replacement target and gives 260.22 iterations/s. Placement 0 now ends at the speculative load-value register after a WB-to-EX lookup. The other placements are limited by a path from the saved raw word through load verification to the divider remainder register.\nRegistered load-table writes passed lint, all 53 formal checks, the cocotb suite, and cosimulation. CoreMark matched the champion’s **3,140,795 cycles**. Median Gowin Fmax was **81.731 MHz**, below the 92.80 MHz replacement threshold.\n\n[Implementation notes](cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
