{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r9s0.yaml && git branch -a && ls -la .tmp'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261123-001-r9s0\ntitle: Register ADD and ADDI separately from the other EX results\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Both completed round-eight designs reported a path from the register file\n  through the ALU to the EX/MEM result register. In a rerun of the champion's\n  74.162 MHz placement, the second timing path passes through an adder and\n  six more LUTs before reaching that register. ADDI already needs the same\n  forwarded-base-plus-immediate sum that EX computes for memory addressing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split EX result selection across the EX/MEM edge. Register one-hot result\n  controls in ID. In EX compute rs1 + rs2 and rs1 + imm in parallel. Mask\n  the first sum for ADD and the second for ADDI, then OR them into one\n  32-bit register. Reuse the effective-address sum for the immediate term.\n  A second register captures the OR of the individually enabled SUB, Boolean,\n  comparison, shift, LUI, AUIPC, jump-link and completed divide results.\n  Feed the bitwise OR of the two registers to EX/MEM forwarding and to MEM.\n  The ADD carry chain now ends at its own register after a two-term select.\n\n  Exclude jumps and AUIPC from the ordinary ADD enables. A divide result is\n  consumed only on response transfer. Qualify each use with the existing\n  producer controls and pipeline validity. The two result registers can\n  sample every clock because the only EX/MEM holds are external memory\n  transactions. A held store consumes its registered address and store data,\n  and a held load supplies its value through the separate load bypass or WB.\n  The replay and divide bubbles suppress register writes as before.\n\n  A scratch implementation completed ten CRC-validated iterations in\n  3,207,017 bracketed cycles. Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 75.044,\n  76.687 and 76.687 MHz, yielding 239.12 iterations/s. This is a 3.4%\n  gain over the champion. The 4.6% replacement margin requires a median\n  above 77.574 MHz at this cycle count. The median placement's longest\n  path now lies inside the divider.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the individual result enables in the ID/EX payload.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Decode the result enables from the validated operation, capture them with its instruction, and retain them across a hold.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Register the two masked sums in one word and the other enabled results in a second word, then OR them onto the existing ALU-result bus.\n* bench-v2.8.4\ntotal 628\ndrwxrwx--T+  5 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 23 05:17 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 15 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 22 23:43 ..\nprw-------+  1 nobody nogroup      0 Nov 23 03:35 GMfifo2844334\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 23 05:11 agent-logs\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   2225 Nov 22 22:45 env.json\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 597005 Nov 23 05:19 orchestrator.log\ndrwxr-x---  11 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 22 22:45 riscv-formal-eval\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 22 22:45 sandbox-probe\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
