^s,\n  so q*Dlo < D. Thus R > -D. A negative R needs exactly one decrement of\n  q and one addition of D to R. This yields exact DIV and REM for every\n  divisor in the large class.\n\n  Keep the current request/response cadence. For large D, use setup to\n  register the scaled opera\n…[1997 of 5069 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:05e4ac89a234f428]…\n: Implement the shared 20-bit trials, fixed-shift scaling and registered unsigned 16-by-16 correction product. Handle D=0 explicitly and retain reset cancellation, stable pending responses and the ALTOPS protocol.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture divider completion fields separately at EX/MEM and qualify their consumption with the advancing divide. Preserve request replay, saved operands and WB interlocks.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the divide operation, sign and completion fields needed for corrected writeback through EX/MEM.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Finish the quotient decrement or remainder restoration and sign selection before MEM/WB. Use the same completed value for retirement and register-file writeback.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Check all five scaling thresholds and their neighbors, cases with and without correction, maximum low-part products, signed overflow, zero divisors and held responses against exact integer arithmetic.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
