{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-002-r15s1.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261123-002-r15s1\ntitle: Read the raw load-cache word in decode and format it in execute\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,140,795 marker cycles at 88.718 MHz. Its reported\n  worst path ends at the 64-bit load-table write port. Pipelining fills in\n  round 14 exposed another path from WB through operand forwarding and the\n  EX index adders to the next table lookup. Both paths arise because EX\n  addresses the table just one edge before a dependent needs a formatted\n  value. Looking up a raw word one stage earlier gives formatting its own\n  cycle and removes the need to store a second copy of the subword.\nhypothesis: |\n  Start the 256-row direct-mapped lookup in ID. Form a tentative word\n  index from the decoded load's register-file base and I-immediate. Use\n  short independent sums of bits [9:5] and [4:2], as in the champion.\n  Read a synchronous RAM containing only the 32-bit raw word and its\n  10-bit tag. Capture the candidate index and occupancy with the RAM\n  output at ID/EX. A base that still needs forwarding can select the wrong\n  row. MEM validates the sampled tag and index against the complete\n  effective address computed with the youngest forwarded base.\n\n  During the load's EX cycle, select and extend bytes from the registered\n  raw word using the true low address bits and decoded width and signedness.\n  Register that result at EX/MEM. A dependent can consume this register\n  immediately, while MEM verifies the address, alignment and occupancy.\n  Use the very same formatted bits for WB on a hit and the captured raw\n  word for RVFI. Every format can hit a resident word on its first use.\n  On a miss, complete from the accepted bus response and replay a\n  dependent through WB. This removes the saved format signature, redundant\n  byte comparisons and internal refresh writes.\n\n  Install raw data directly from completed cacheable bus reads or aligned\n  full-word stores. Invalidate on an accepted narrow RAM store. Carry\n  validity with the instruction and reject any same-index update from\n  the read edge through the edge on which the load leaves EX, including\n  updates while ID/EX is held. This makes stale samples and RAM port\n  collisions ordinary misses. Flush wrong-path candidates, clear validity\n  on reset and retain the existing MMIO, trap and retirement behavior.\n\n  Measure index mismatches and collision misses between the CoreMark\n  markers alongside median Gowin Fmax. At the champion's cycle count\n  the acceptance gate is 92.80 MHz. A target of 95 MHz with at most 1%\n  more cycles yields about 299.5 iterations/s. The risk is that a\n  register-file read followed by the ID index sum becomes the new limit.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Form the tentative row index from the current decode base and displacement. Align its lookup with ID/EX acceptance, holds and flushes.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Carry the decode lookup, stage advance signals and candidate data between ID, the load table and EX. Preserve replay gating on dependent side effects.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Use a synchronous raw-word and tag RAM, track intervening row updates, verify the candidate at MEM and drive hit writeback and RVFI from the same sample. Fill directly from accepted bus reads and full-word stores.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Format the decode-stage raw candidate with the forwarded low address bits and register the value, raw word and lookup metadata on EX advance.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the registered load sample, formatted result and verification metadata at the EX/MEM boundary.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Cover adjacent loads at different byte offsets and signedness, a stale decode base, same-row stores at both intervening edges, a held or flushed lookup, and an MMIO address with matching low bits. Check dependent values and bus handshakes.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
