{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-002-r8s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261123-002-r8s1\ntitle: Pipeline successor-table accesses off the execute-to-fetch control path\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  At 70.620 MHz and 3,207,017 cycles for ten iterations, the champion's reported worst path starts in the register file, crosses EX and ends at the fetch successor BRAM. Both other round-seven designs reported paths ending at the table's occupancy bits. Today the same late accept signal controls the synchronous read, row installation and occupancy update. Moving those memory operations across a register boundary could raise Fmax while preserving one fetch per clock.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split successor lookup and installation into independent pipelines inside IF. Read the existing 512-row BRAM every clock from the current PC. Register whether fetch actually advanced. When it did, use the fresh read result. On the first hold or redirect, retain the preceding candidate and its validity in a shadow register so it remains available across repeated holds. Capture that shadow from the previous cycle's registered selection. Keep the full successor-PC check and live instruction priority.\n\n  Capture each accepted live fill as a one-entry write pipeline carrying the predecessor index, successor PC, word, decoded target and branch flags. Commit one registered fill per clock to both BRAM and occupancy. Align the read-valid bit with the row actually read and mask same-address BRAM read/write collisions. Reset and FENCE.I must squash pending fills and candidates, including the shadow. Register the bulk occupancy clear and suppress candidate validity until it takes effect. EX still corrects the fetch PC on its existing edge. Only local registered controls should reach the table ports and the occupancy write network.\n\n  A median above 73.87 MHz at the champion's cycle count would clear the acceptance gate. Check the vendor path endpoints and the bracketed cycle count separately to see whether this retiming achieves that gain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Add the unconditional synchronous lookup, retained candidate, registered fill transaction and ordered validity updates around the existing successor table.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
