{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261123-003-r12s2.last; cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r12s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261123-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Rotate load-predictor rows to put the last accessed lane on the bypass\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's reported path starts at saved_raw in the load predictor and\n  ends at the EX/MEM result register. A narrow hit currently compares a saved\n  formatted value with the raw bytes before releasing the consumer. The two\n  representations cost 17 extra bits per row and put byte comparisons on the\n  replay path. Round nine observed 65,415 repeated-format hits in 83,971\n  adjacent subword uses. That locality can select a byte lane at fill time.\nhypothesis: |\n  Store each resident word once, with its four bytes cyclically rotated so the\n  byte at the last load's offset occupies bits 7:0. Record that two-bit offset\n  beside the ordinary address tag. Aligned SW and LW fills use offset zero.\n  Form the speculative value from fixed slices of this word. LB/LBU use its\n  low byte, LH/LHU its low half and LW all 32 bits. Apply the issuing load's\n  width and signedness and register the candidate for its dependent consumer.\n  MEM verifies the complete word address, occupancy, alignment, collision\n  status and equality of the stored and requested offsets. Signed and unsigned\n  loads at the same offset can share a prediction. The canonical raw word and\n  bypass now come from the same bytes, removing the redundant data comparison.\n\n  On a word-address hit with a different offset, undo the stored rotation,\n  finish the load internally and refresh the row in the requested orientation.\n  Replay an adjacent dependent instruction through WB on this first access.\n  Use the inverse rotation for the RVFI raw word on every internal completion.\n  A tag miss uses the accepted bus word. Invalidate on accepted narrow stores,\n  exclude MMIO, and suppress same-row read/write collisions as today.\n\n  The projected gain comes primarily from removing the saved-data checks from\n  replay and reducing row width from 64 to 44 bits. At the champion's\n  3,140,795 cycles the replacement threshold requires about 87.3 MHz.\n  Measure the cycle cost of changing row orientation together with median\n  Gowin Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Store the tagged rotated word and offset, derive both the predicted operand and MEM raw word from it, and refresh on a verified word with a mismatched lane.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Route the producer's load width and signedness alongside the existing speculative row index so MEM can register its fixed-slice bypass candidate.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise all four byte orientations, alternating signedness, halfword and word promotion, a same-row collision, and a dependent branch during an external stall. Check load masks, raw words, register results and retirement PCs.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
