{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -1 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c 1-6000 && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261123-003-r7s2.last'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261123-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Complete division in MEM with four quotient bits per clock\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin traces the champion's 20.904 ns, 102-cell setup path from\\nquotient_q[34] to remainder_q[9]. Three serial radix-4 digit selections\\nsit between those registers. CoreMark retires zero divides between its\\ntiming markers. Letting a divide occupy MEM while it runs buys a clock\\nfor a shallower recurrence within the existing formal progress bound.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Gowin traces the champion's 20.904 ns, 102-cell setup path from\\nquotient_q[34] to remainder_q[9]. Three serial radix-4 digit selections\\nsit between those registers. CoreMark retires zero divides between its\\ntiming markers. Letting a divide occupy MEM while it runs buys a clock\\nfor a shallower recurrence within the existing formal progress bound.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Launch DIV/REM from the forwarded operands as EX advances. Move the\\ninstruction and its RVFI operands into EX/MEM on that same edge. MEM owns\\nthe instruction until the divider response transfers directly into\\nMEM/WB. An immediately dependent instruction uses the existing WB-only\\ninterlock. This takes sign restoration off the ordinary EX result mux.\\n\\nIn the setup clock, compute 3D from the registered divisor magnitude D\\nand consume the top nibble N of the dividend magnitude. For D >= 16 the\\nprefix quotient is zero and the remainder is N. Otherwise read a\\n256-by-8 constant ROM addressed by {D[3:0], N}. Pack floor(N/D) in\\nthe high nibble and N mod D in the low nibble. Entries for D=0 return\\nfour one bits followed by N.\\nSeed the 32-bit shift register with {dividend[27:0], prefix_quotient}\\nand zero-extend the prefix remainder. Seven clocks of two radix-4\\ndigits each consume the remaining 28 bits exactly. Each digit tests\\nD, 2D and registered 3D in parallel with 35-bit borrow-producing\\nsubtracts and selects the residual using the 2D borrow first.\\n\\nA scratch implementation ran ten validated CoreMark iterations in\\n3,20\n…[3435 of 6507 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1bb828ed3cdf1552]…\ngnitudes on issue. Initialize the nibble ROM at elaboration,\\nthen capture the selected prefix and 3D together on the setup edge.\\nAn eight-bit one-hot phase register sequences setup and seven rounds.\\nRestore the quotient or remainder sign from the saved operation and\\noperand signs. Keep divide-by-zero and signed overflow exact.\\nUse the same eight-clock response schedule under\\nALTOPS. Hold the result under backpressure and allow a new request\\non the edge that consumes a previous response. Reset cancels both\nWrote and schema-validated the [predictor hypothesis](cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r7s2.yaml). It proposes reading four load-value predictor banks in parallel and registering their formatted results before selecting the consumer’s operand.\n\nThe single-bank prototype saved **81,075 CoreMark cycles** and reached **210.48 iterations/s**. The proposed four-bank design needs more than **67.334 MHz** to clear the tournament margin. Its estimated **6% fitness gain** remains unverified.", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
