{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r9s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261123-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Predict the load bypass value with one formatted value per word\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current word predictor lets an LW consumer execute immediately, but every\n  adjacent byte or halfword consumer waits for WB. Servicing all widths saved\n  81,075 of 3,207,017 marker cycles in round seven. Round eight's asymmetric\n  RAM prototype achieved the same cycle count, but its forwarding and WB\n  paths reconstructed the same value differently and the register consistency\n  proof timed out. The current median placement also puts the register-file\n  RAM output and several layers of operand selection on the critical EX path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict that a subword load will reuse the byte offset, width and signedness\n  of the last subword load to the same resident word. Keep the raw word and\n  one already extended 32-bit value with its format signature in the same\n  synchronous predictor row. A read miss fills the row from the accepted RAM\n  response. A subword hit on the right word with a different signature\n  computes the architectural value once in MEM and refreshes the saved\n  format. A full-word store installs its raw word and clears the signature.\n  Invalidate on an accepted narrow store. Preserve reset, collision and\n  full-address checks, including exclusion of MMIO.\n\n  Pick the raw field for LW and the formatted field for narrow loads using\n  the producer's registered width. Feed that candidate directly to a dependent\n  EX operand. In parallel MEM verifies the tag and index, alignment and, for\n  narrow loads, the signature. On success the identical candidate drives WB.\n  On a signature miss the verified raw word can still complete the load\n  internally. Hold and retry an actual dependent consumer from WB on either\n  kind of miss, suppressing its redirects, training and side effects until\n  it can advance. Raw data and masks continue to supply RVFI. Keep the\n  speculative load source as a parallel one-hot term with the three ordinary\n  forwarding sources so the register-file path through EX avoids the existing\n  final load-select mux.\n\n  Count signature hits specifically at adjacent dependent subword uses in\n  the marker window. Measure marker cycles and median Gowin Fmax together.\n  At 3.15 million cycles the design needs just over 76.2 MHz to clear the\n  4.6 percent replacement threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep raw and formatted data together, train and verify the format signature, and supply the verified bypass value to WB.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Remove the subword-use interlock and qualify dependent replay with formatted-value verification.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Forward the candidate through the existing per-source one-hot network and retain the replay suppression of side effects.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise repeated and changing byte and halfword signatures, store invalidation, exact RVFI masks and values, and held or replayed consumers.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
