{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat bench/programs/Makefile; rg -n '([\"'^/ ])[ ]*/[ ]*[''^/*=]|[[:alnum:]_)][ ]+%[ ]+[[:alnum:]_(]'\"' bench/programs/coremark/core_{list_join,matrix,state,main}.c\"", "aggregated_output": "CROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_state.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_util.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.c \\\n        bench/programs/crt0.S\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: $(SRCS)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $^ -o $@\n\nbench/programs/selftest.elf: bench/programs/selftest.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n# Random full-trace programs (V2). The .S files are generated once by\n# gen_random_trace.py <seed> and committed, so every candidate runs the\n# same programs.\nRANDOM_ELFS := bench/programs/random1.elf bench/programs/random2.elf bench/programs/random3.elf\n\nbench/programs/random%.elf: bench/programs/random%.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n.PHONY: all clean\nall: bench/programs/coremark.elf bench/programs/selftest.elf $(RANDOM_ELFS)\nclean:\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:8:    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:205:        results[i].size = results[i].size / num_algorithms;\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:262:        results[0].iterations *= 1 + 10 / divisor;\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:363:        ee_printf(\"Iterations/Sec   : %f\\n\",\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:369:        ee_printf(\"Iterations/Sec   : %d\\n\",\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:409:            ee_printf(\"CoreMark 1.0 : %f / %s %s\",\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:415:            ee_printf(\" / %s\", MEM_LOCATION);\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:417:            ee_printf(\" / %s\", mem_name[MEM_METHOD]);\nbench/programs/coremark/core_main.c:421:            ee_printf(\" / %d:%s\", default_num_contexts, PARALLEL_METHOD);\nbench/programs/coremark/core_state.c:8:    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\nbench/programs/coremark/core_state.c:32:the switch/if behaviour, we are using a small moore machine.\nbench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c:8:    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\nbench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c:155:        - Single remove/reinsert\nbench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c:255:    ee_u32 size     = (blksize / per_item)\nbench/progr