{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-001-r3s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; r=json.loads(sys.stdin.readline()); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"motivation\\\"]); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"changes\\\"]); print(r[\\\"seeds\\\"],r[\\\"critical_path\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"The champion's worst path on Gowin placement option 0 runs from the\nregister file through the multiplier DSP and EX result mux to a data\nRAM address pin, with a reported arrival time of 27.311 ns. This path\nexists because dmem_addr takes the general EX/MEM alu_result. Every\nRV32IM load and store needs only forwarded rs1 plus its immediate.\n\nRegister the full 32-bit sum rs1 + in.imm alongside the general result\nat EX/MEM. This sum is already used for JALR in EX. Driving the memory\naddress and byte-lane logic from that register removes the DSP and the\ngeneral result mux from the RAM address path without adding a cycle.\n\nA scratch implementation reached 48.319, 49.590 and 49.590 MHz across\nthe three Gowin placements, up from the champion's 45.640 MHz median.\nWith both buses stalled pseudo-randomly, ten CoreMark iterations passed\nCRC validation in 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, matching the champion.\nTogether these measurements give 110.41 iterations/s, an 8.66% gain\nover 101.61. Placement option 0 used 636 registers, up from 604.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add a 32-bit effective_addr field immediately after alu_result in ex_mem_t.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register post-forwarding rs1 plus in.imm directly into effective_addr\\non the normal EX/MEM advance edge. Hold it with the memory controls\\nand store data during dmem backpressure.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use effective_addr for dmem_addr, misalignment detection, byte masks,\\nload extraction and the aligned RVFI memory address. Continue using\\nthe general ALU result for register writeback and forwarding.\\n'}]\n[48.319, 49.59, 49.59] {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -15.696, 'arrival_ns': 25.99, 'logic_cells': 18, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
