{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"du -sh formal/riscv-formal/ && ls formal/riscv-formal/ && cat formal/checks_si.cfg && sed -n '67,193p' formal/run_all.sh\"", "aggregated_output": "201M\tformal/riscv-formal/\nCOPYING\nCodeOfConduct\nREADME.md\nbus\nchecks\ncores\ndocs\ninsns\nmonitor\ntests\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n# Hold a lock on the work dir for this run's lifetime. The reaper below\n# only removes dirs whose lock nobody holds; flock works across users and\n# PID namespaces, unlike the old `kill -0 <pid>` test (from inside a\n# sandbox every outside PID looks dead). Without flock(1), nothing is reaped.\nHAVE_FLOCK=\nif command -v flock >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    exec 9>\"$CORE_DIR/.owner.lock\"\n    flock 9\n    HAVE_FLOCK=1\nfi\n\n# Auto-detect single-issue cores from core.yaml when WRAPPER + CHECKS_CFG\n# are both uns\n…[3725 of 6797 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19cb72a817a45986]…\nl [verilog-files] section\n# and rebuild from the glob, with core_pkg.sv first and wrapper.sv last.\nSTAGED_CFG=\"$CORE_DIR/checks.cfg\"\nawk '/^\\[verilog-files\\]/{exit} {print}' \"$CHECKS_CFG\" > \"$STAGED_CFG\"\n{\n    echo \"[verilog-files]\"\n    [ -f \"$CORE_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && \\\n        echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/core_pkg.sv\"\n    for f in \"$CORE_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n        name=\"$(basename \"$f\")\"\n        [ \"$name\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n        [ \"$name\" = \"wrapper.sv\" ] && continue\n        echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/$name\"\n    done\n    echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\"\n} >> \"$STAGED_CFG\"\n\n# genchecks.py derives @core@ from the cwd's basename (genchecks.py:39),\n# so cd-ing into $CORE_DIR (= $RISCV_FORMAL/cores/$CORE_NAME-<suffix>)\n# yields @core@=\"$CORE_NAME-<suffix>\". The [verilog-files] lines we just\n# wrote reference that @core@, so all paths resolve into this private dir.\ncd \"$CORE_DIR\"\nrm -rf checks/\necho \"=== genchecks ===\" | tee -a \"$LOG\"\npython3 ../../checks/genchecks.py >> \"$LOG\" 2>&1\ncd checks\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
