{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated the [structural divider hypothesis](cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r2s1.yaml).\n\nIt targets the champion’s 37.434 ns divider feedback path by reducing eight serial subtraction decisions to three radix-4 selections per clock. CoreMark executes no divisions between its timing markers. At the current cycle count, **41.4 MHz would yield 92.2 iterations/s**, a projected 30% gain over 70.94.\n\nThe proposed arithmetic matched a reference model on 10,100 operand pairs. FPGA timing remains unmeasured."}}
