{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261122-002-r2s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Fold DIV and REM into a four-round execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through operand forwarding and the EX ALU. The baseline puts full-width signed and unsigned division and remainder in the ALU result mux. These operators are the most likely source of its depth. A reference-interpreter run of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration ELF matched all five CRCs. Of 2,922,015 instructions retired between the marker writes, 93,960 were MUL and zero were DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through operand forwarding and the EX ALU. The baseline puts full-width signed and unsigned division and remainder in the ALU result mux. These operators are the most likely source of its depth. A reference-interpreter run of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration ELF matched all five CRCs. Of 2,922,015 instructions retired between the marker writes, 93,960 were MUL and zero were DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four combinational DIV/REM operations with one blocking restoring divider. Capture forwarded operands and their signs on issue. Compute eight quotient bits per clock for four clocks, registering the quotient and partial remainder after each round. Select and sign-correct the result on transfer to EX/MEM. The ordinary ALU and multiplier keep their current latency and forwarding paths. Only a valid divide or remainder instruction incurs the extra cycles.\\n\\nThe instruction counts predict zero divider wait cycles in the measured interval. At the baseline's 4,491,485 marker cycles, a median Fmax of 5.70 MHz would clear the acceptance threshold and 8.17 MHz would deliver about 18.2 iterations/s. Check the cycle count and median Fmax separately. The multiplier and the eight-step divider round are candidates for the new longest path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"descrip\n…[8998 of 12070 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:599b10bfa2cedcd2]…\nultiples.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 101.61, \"delta_pct\": 43.23, \"vs_baseline\": 738.37, \"fmax_mhz\": 45.64, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2960, \"ff\": 604, \"seeds\": [45.421, 45.64, 45.64], \"perturbations\": [[0, 45.421, 16], [1, 45.64, 23], [2, 45.64, 23]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -17.016, \"arrival_ns\": 27.311, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T22:11:00.004451Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r2s1 (improvement, +43.23%): Registering 3D in a setup cycle let each radix-4 digit test D, 2D and 3D in parallel, raising Fmax by cutting the divider's remainder feedback path from eight dependent subtract/select stages to three.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
