or other instructions, including JALR. Use raw instruction bits for\n  prediction so the EX squash signal is outside the prediction datapath.\n\n  Capture one predicted-taken bit and the counter snapshot on the same edge\n  that accepts the instruction. Train a conditional branch once when valid\n  EX advances, with saturation toward its forwarded, resolved direction.\n  For direct trans\n…[1288 of 4360 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5c960e5da86b5ea0]…\nthrough if_id_t and id_ex_t.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture prediction metadata with its instruction. Clear valid and side-effect controls on a bubble or recovery and retain them on a hold.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Resolve the direction mismatch, supply the architectural recovery PC and emit one conditional training event per advancing branch using its PC and saved counter.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire EX recovery and training back to fetch while preserving the single-retire interface.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Apply EX correction at the PC and ID/EX capture boundary. Give dmem holds priority over squash and let recovery override an unready instruction bus on release.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check consecutive branch and target retirements after loop warmup, aliased counters, a loop exit, JAL links, JALR and misaligned targets. Overlap recovery with bus stalls and check that a wrong-path store never reaches dmem.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
