{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r10s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261123-001-r10s0\ntitle: Pipeline the 256-entry load-table occupancy lookup in two dimensions\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The EX operand mux and two partial address adders currently feed an\n  indexed read of 256 resettable occupied bits before the EX/MEM edge.\n  The load's full address and format are checked in MEM. Only MEM needs\n  the selected occupancy bit, so the final selection can move across\n  that edge. This targets the timing of the verified load bypass while\n  retaining coverage of all 256 words.\nhypothesis: |\n  Arrange the occupancy bits as 16 groups of 16 rows in distributed RAM.\n  Keep a resettable initialized bit per group. Read the addressed group\n  and capture its 16-bit mask, initialized flag and lookup index with the\n  data candidate. In MEM use the registered low index bits to select the\n  row's occupied bit in parallel with full-address and format verification.\n  Hold the entire sample through data-bus backpressure.\n  \n  On the first update to a group, start from a zero mask. Set the addressed\n  bit for an installation and clear it for an accepted narrow store.\n  Reset invalidates every group and the in-flight candidate. Preserve the\n  same-row collision veto on concurrent lookup and update. A different-row\n  update within the same group preserves the bit being read.\n  \n  A scratch implementation reached 77.475, 80.815 and 80.815 MHz across\n  the three Gowin placements. Placement 0 used 6,295 logic cells and\n  1,123 registers, down from 6,616 and 1,346. At the champion's cycle\n  count the measured median gives 257.31 iterations/s. The acceptance\n  target is above 261.02 iterations/s, or 81.981 MHz at that cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Replace the flat occupied vector with group masks and resettable group flags. Register the addressed mask and collision qualification beside each lookup and select the row in MEM.\n'''.replace('  \\\\n','\\\\n'))\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
