{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r11s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-001-r11s0\ntitle: Write the final radix-16 digit back into the divider state\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Repeating the champion's 83.455 MHz Gowin placement exposed a path from\n  quotient_q[30] through a trial subtraction to EX/MEM alu_result[12].\n  The divider already has registers for the quotient and remainder, and the\n  completed divide spends a full cycle in MEM before WB samples its result.\n  Isolating the response from the EX integer-result mux is worth testing.\n  A scratch cut that registered four partial remainders at EX/MEM reached\n  85.274 MHz on placement option 1, at the cost of four 32-bit data paths.\nhypothesis: |\n  On a DIV/REM response handshake, clock the eighth digit through the same\n  quotient shift and remainder feedback registers that capture digits two\n  through seven. Capture all 32 remainder bits on this edge. The next trial\n  still takes only remainder_q[27:0] and the next dividend nibble as inputs.\n  During the following MEM cycle, select the completed quotient or remainder\n  directly from those registers and apply the existing sign correction.\n  This removes the final trial and its transfer enable from the common EX\n  result mux without introducing a separate wide result pipeline.\n  \n  A divide in MEM always advances at the next edge. A following divide\n  can overwrite the state on that edge, when MEM/WB has already sampled\n  the older value. Hold the seventh-digit state while a response is blocked\n  and perform the final feedback update exactly once on acceptance. Keep\n  the ALU's pre-handshake result available to its existing callers. In\n  ALTOPS mode expose the request-latched substitute result to MEM for the\n  same interval. Retain the WB dependency interlock and saved RVFI operands.\n  \n  Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,140,795 marker cycles in the champion.\n  At that count a median above 87.29 MHz is needed to clear the 4.6% gate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Capture the last quotient digit and full remainder on response transfer and provide the registered magnitude for MEM in real and ALTOPS modes.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the decoded divide-result select and its sign through EX/MEM.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Keep the fast ALU result independent of the divide response and export the divider's registered magnitude.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect the registered divider output to the MEM result selector.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Select and sign-correct the registered divide magnitude at the MEM/WB edge.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check adjacent independent divides and remainders with different signs, a dependent consumer, divide by zero, and a stalled older memory access.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r11s0.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('valid',265.71*1.046*3.140795/10)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
