{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith('r9s2') or d['id'].endswith('r8s0'):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],d.get('error'))\nPY\nrg -n 'critical|retaining|keep' cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-001-r8s0 Reorganize the existing 256-row verified word table so a producer selects\nthe format while addressing the RAMs. Each accepted fill writes all byte\nlanes of the source word and their precomputed sign extensions together.\nEach narrow read port returns exactly the fragment required at its position\nin the 32-bit result. Concatenate the three registered outputs directly\ninto the existing speculative load bypass.\n\nUse an 8-bit low port with four choices per row. Use an 8-bit middle port\nwhose slots 0 and 1 hold bytes 1 and 3, slots 2 and 3 hold zero, and\nslots 4 through 7 hold the four byte-sign masks. The 16-bit upper port\nholds the raw upper half in slot 0, zeros in slots 1 through 3 and the\nfour replicated sign bits in slots 4 through 7. The byte lane comes from\nthe exact low two address bits. For signed halfwords the sign\ncomes from byte 1 or byte 3. A word read selects byte 0, byte 1 and the\nupper half. Infer the asymmetric ports with one indexed synchronous read\nand parallel writes to constant subindices of the same word row.\n\nFull-address, occupancy, alignment and read/write-collision checks in MEM\nauthorize consumption. A failed dependent load follows the existing hold,\nbubble and WB replay protocol. The raw word still supplies RVFI. Keep the\nmultiply-use interlock and the verified-hit behavior under bus stalls.\n\nA scratch prototype ran ten CRC-validated iterations in 3,125,942 cycles\nand matched the ISS on selftest and three random programs with ready and\nstalled buses. All 30 directed pipeline cases passed with the new one-cycle\nhit expectation and additional signed and unsigned lane cases. Gowin\nplacements 0, 1 and 2 reached 68.473, 70.609 and 70.609 MHz. The median\ngives 225.88 iterations/s, a 2.58% gain. Placement 0 used 17 of the 46\nBSRAMs, up from 10, and 4,683 logic cells, down from 4,824. The 4.6% margin\nrequires 72.00 MHz at this cycle count. The median placement's critical\npath runs from the raw word/tag RAM, through load verification and replay,\nto register-file read control.\n \n…[2738 of 5810 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7a4bb5d3a9cefa13]…\nIO.\n\nPick the raw field for LW and the formatted field for narrow loads using\nthe producer's registered width. Feed that candidate directly to a dependent\nEX operand. In parallel MEM verifies the tag and index, alignment and, for\nnarrow loads, the signature. On success the identical candidate drives WB.\nOn a signature miss the verified raw word can still complete the load\ninternally. Hold and retry an actual dependent consumer from WB on either\nkind of miss, suppressing its redirects, training and side effects until\nit can advance. Raw data and masks continue to supply RVFI. Keep the\nspeculative load source as a parallel one-hot term with the three ordinary\nforwarding sources so the register-file path through EX avoids the existing\nfinal load-select mux.\n\nCount signature hits specifically at adjacent dependent subword uses in\nthe marker window. Measure marker cycles and median Gowin Fmax together.\nAt 3.15 million cycles the design needs just over 76.2 MHz to clear the\n4.6 percent replacement threshold.\n None\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
