{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor a in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if a.get('id','').endswith(('r9s2','r12s2','r13s2')): print(a['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Predict that a subword load will reuse the byte offset, width and signedness\nof the last subword load to the same resident word. Keep the raw word and\none already extended 32-bit value with its format signature in the same\nsynchronous predictor row. A read miss fills the row from the accepted RAM\nresponse. A subword hit on the right word with a different signature\ncomputes the architectural value once in MEM and refreshes the saved\nformat. A full-word store installs its raw word and clears the signature.\nInvalidate on an accepted narrow store. Preserve reset, collision and\nfull-address checks, including exclusion of MMIO.\n\nPick the raw field for LW and the formatted field for narrow loads using\nthe producer's registered width. Feed that candidate directly to a dependent\nEX operand. In parallel MEM verifies the tag and index, alignment and, for\nnarrow loads, the signature. On success the identical candidate drives WB.\nOn a signature miss the verified raw word can still complete the load\ninternally. Hold and retry an actual dependent consumer from WB on either\nkind of miss, suppressing its redirects, training and side effects until\nit can advance. Raw data and masks continue to supply RVFI. Keep the\nspeculative load source as a parallel one-hot term with the three ordinary\nforwarding sources so the register-file path through EX avoids the existing\nfinal load-select mux.\n\nCount signature hits specifically at adjacent dependent subword uses in\nthe marker window. Measure marker cycles and median Gowin Fmax together.\nAt 3.15 million cycles the design needs just over 76.2 MHz to clear the\n4.6 percent replacement threshold.\n\nStore each resident word once, with its four bytes cyclically rotated so the\nbyte at the last load's offset occupies bits 7:0. Record that two-bit offset\nbeside the ordinary address tag. Aligned SW and LW fills use offset zero.\nForm the speculative value from fixed slices of this word. LB/LBU use its\nlow byte, LH/LHU its low half and LW all 32 bits. Apply the issuing load's\nwidth and signedness and r\n…[1586 of 4658 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0579bd89a382ecba]…\nrm Hnew, and write Hnew back. Register two ten-bit\npattern indices, PC[11:2] XOR (H << 2) and PC[11:2] XOR (Hnew << 2).\nUpdate the saturating counter at the old index. Publish the sign bit of\nthe counter at the new index in the PC's fast direction array. If the\nindices coincide, publish the just-trained MSB. Initialize history and\ndirection to zero and counters to weakly not taken. The update pipeline\naccepts one resolution per clock. A rapid revisit can see an older hint\nand EX still recovers on a mismatch.\n\nIn scratch RTL the ten-iteration bracket fell from 3,140,795 to 3,116,418\ncycles with both stalls enabled and all five CRCs validated. At this cycle\ncount a median above 86.62 MHz clears the 277.93 iterations/s threshold.\nThe only fetch-side predictor read is the direction bit. Holds, replays\nand invalid slots cannot produce a training event. Gate pending writes\non reset. Count misses and cycles between the MMIO markers and use the\nmedian of Gowin's three placement options to test the throughput claim.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
