{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor a in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if a.get('id','').endswith(('r8s0','r10s0','r11s2','r6s1')): print(a['id'],a['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-002-r6s1 Move forwarding arbitration across the ID/EX register. For each source, decode\nselects the youngest effective writer and registers a one-hot mask that names\nwhere its value will be in the following cycle. EX forms each operand by ORing\nthe masked data buses. Give raw word-load data its own input so an aligned LW\nand its immediate consumer can advance on successive clocks. Give the ALU\ninputs their own registered masks with PC and immediate choices so those muxes\nalso resolve in decode. Byte and halfword loads and multiplies use the existing\nWB interlock.\n\nA scratch prototype on this champion completed ten iterations in 3,344,675\nmarker cycles with all five CRCs correct. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2\nreached 63.152, 65.278 and 65.278 MHz. The median gives 195.17 iterations/s,\n12.57 percent above the champion. The prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks.\n\nhyp-20261123-001-r8s0 Reorganize the existing 256-row verified word table so a producer selects\nthe format while addressing the RAMs. Each accepted fill writes all byte\nlanes of the source word and their precomputed sign extensions together.\nEach narrow read port returns exactly the fragment required at its position\nin the 32-bit result. Concatenate the three registered outputs directly\ninto the existing speculative load bypass.\n\nUse an 8-bit low port with four choices per row. Use an 8-bit middle port\nwhose slots 0 and 1 hold bytes 1 and 3, slots 2 and 3 hold zero, and\nslots 4 through 7 hold the four byte-sign masks. The 16-bit upper port\nholds the raw upper half in slot 0, zeros in slots 1 through 3 and the\nfour replicated sign bits in slots 4 through 7. The byte lane comes from\nthe exact low two address bits. For signed halfwords the sign\ncomes from byte 1 or byte 3. A word read selects byte 0, byte 1 and the\nupper half. Infer the asymmetric ports with one indexed synchronous read\nand parallel writes to constant subindices of the same word row.\n\nFull-address, occupancy, alignment and read/write-collision checks in MEM\nauthorize con\n…[3284 of 6356 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:567f9c76d3e7c0cf]…\nad's predicted-value bits [9:2]\nor the older non-load's EX/MEM ALU-result bits [9:2]. This source predicts\nzero carries and can be wrong after an older load miss or late M result.\nSelect the four row candidates with the registered rs1 bypass enables.\nThis removes the WB result mux and address arithmetic from the path\nbetween the WB register and the synchronous table read.\n\nHold the WB row with WB data and use the held consumer's displacement\nwhen decode stalls. MEM must match the saved index and tag against the\nfull forwarded effective address and retain every occupancy, collision,\nalignment and format check. Allocate and invalidate using the true\naddress. An incorrect estimate falls through to the existing bus and\ndependent-replay path.\n\nA scratch implementation ran ten CRC-validated iterations in 3,134,538\nbracketed cycles with both buses stalled, versus 3,140,795 for the\nchampion. It needs a median above 87.12 MHz to clear the replacement\nmargin. The fitness estimate depends primarily on that clock gain.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
