{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_31", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor a in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if a.get('id','').endswith(('r7s2','r6s2')): print(a['id'],a['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-003-r6s2 Predict that an LW can supply an immediate consumer through the EX/MEM\nbypass. Remove the initial load-use bubble for LW. In the producer's EX\ncycle, predict an eight-bit word index from the forwarded base and\nsigned offset. Add bits [9:5] modulo 32 and bits [4:2] modulo 8.\nConcatenate the sums and discard carry between fields. Read a 256-entry\nsynchronous table at this index while separately registering the exact\n32-bit effective address. Each row holds a 32-bit raw RAM word and its\nten-bit tag [19:10], with one resettable occupancy bit per row.\n\nIn the following cycle, feed the candidate word directly into the\ndependent instruction's EX operand mux. Use one-hot enables to select\nthe prediction, ordinary EX/MEM result, WB result or captured operand,\nwith the usual youngest-writer priority. In parallel,\nMEM checks validity, alignment and the whole address reconstructed from\nzero high bits, stored tag and captured predicted index. A verified\nhit completes the load even with dmemReady low and suppresses dmemREn.\nByte and halfword loads may use the verified word in MEM with normal\nextraction and sign or zero extension. Their immediate consumers and multiply\nconsumers retain the WB interlock.\n\nOn a miss, read the true bus address and respect backpressure. If the\nyounger EX instruction depends on the load's nonzero rd, hold its ID/EX\nslot and the fetch PC. On response, move the load into WB and insert one\nEX/MEM bubble. Capture any older WB operand needed by the held consumer.\nIt retries locally with the correct WB value on the next cycle. A held\nor replaying consumer must never redirect, train a predictor, start a\ndivide, enter MEM or cause an external store. Independent work can\nadvance with the completing load.\n\nFill from accepted aligned RAM read misses. An accepted aligned SW\ninstalls its own write data. An accepted SB or SH invalidates the\nindexed row. Hold the read candidate across a memory freeze and mask a\nsimultaneous lookup and update of the same row. Reset clears occupancy.\nVerify the\n…[1630 of 4702 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a3392dcad48f2d4d]…\ne and architectural format.\nHold a dependent consumer through backpressure, bubble it once on\ncompletion, and retry from WB. Gate redirect, training, division and\nwrites on successful advance. Preserve collision suppression, reset\ninvalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store invalidation.\nKeep the WB-only multiply interlock.\n\nA single-bank control prototype passed the canonical UART and five CRC checks\nin 3,125,942 marker cycles, saving 81,075 cycles over the champion.\nGowin measured 62.721, 65.795 and 65.795 MHz. The median gives\n210.48 iterations/s, a 2.2% gain. At that cycle count the tournament\nrequires more than 67.334 MHz. The longest median-placement path\nended at the shared EX/MEM result register through the predictor read\nand format logic. All 30 directed pipeline cases passed on the control prototype. The proposed four-bank layout targets 68.25 MHz,\nwhich would give 218.33 iterations/s at the measured cycle count.\nIts post-route clock and the delay of the consumer mux remain unmeasured.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
