{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith(('r3s1','r4s2')): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith(('r3s1','r4s2')): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Put one entry holding a PC, instruction and valid bit between fetch and\ndecode. An empty buffer passes a ready word directly to decode. If decode\nis blocked, save that word and advance the fetch address. A full buffer\ncan issue its head even when imem is stalled, and can refill on the same\nedge. Qualify the ID/EX transfer or bubble with validity and redirect so\nthe redirect signal no longer has to rewrite instruction bits before\nthe source-register comparisons. Sequential issue retains one instruction\nper cycle and an accepted EX redirect discards all younger work.\n\nA scratch prototype on the champion passed all eight RVFI trace comparisons\nacross selftest and three random programs, with and without bus stalls.\nIt passed the canonical CoreMark UART and CRC checks. Ten iterations\ntook 4,353,657 marker cycles, down from\n4,491,485. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 gave 49.530, 51.204 and\n51.204 MHz. The median yields 117.61 iterations/s, 15.75% over 101.61.\nAt the prototype cycle count, a median above 46.273 MHz clears the 4.6%\nacceptance margin.\n\nGive each accepted fetch one prediction of its successor instruction.\nRead a 256-entry synchronous RAM indexed by the source PC[9:2]. Each\nrow holds the last observed successor's 18-bit word address and 32-bit\ninstruction. This read starts in parallel with the existing branch\ndirection lookup and target calculation. Keep the registered fetch PC\nas the external imem address and as the authority for validating the guess.\n\nOn the next cycle, select live bus data whenever imemReady is high.\nOtherwise issue the saved word only if the candidate is valid and\n{12'b0, saved_word_address, 2'b00} equals the entire current fetch PC.\nSource-index aliases are safe because the stored word was fetched at\nthat exact successor address. A wrong guess with an unready bus holds\nthe PC for a real response.\nFeed the selected word to decode, load-use detection and direct-branch\nprediction. Use bus-ready OR validated-hit as fetch availability.\n\nRetain the preceding accepted PC's row index and a predecessor-valid bit.\nWhen decode accepts an in-range aligned bus word without an EX squash,\nwrite its address and bits into that predecessor's row. An instruction\nsupplied by prediction can become a predecessor. Read the current PC's\nrow and capture its validity on each acceptance. Suppress the candidate\non a simultaneous read and write to the same row. Hold the candidate\nand predecessor through retries, data-memory stalls, divide holds and\nbranch recovery so the corrected successor can train the same source.\nEX resolves transfers and overrides fetch backpressure as in the champion.\n\nReset clears the 256 occupancy bits, predecessor-valid and candidate-valid.\nAn advancing FENCE.I clears them again and squashes the younger fetch,\nrestarting at the fence's PC+4 after older stores complete. Both cases\nleave the wide RAM contents available for block RAM inference.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
