{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r5s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-001-r5s0\ntitle: Forward word and halfword loads directly from the memory stage\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  An instruction that consumes a load currently waits one cycle for WB,\n  even when the data bus can return the value in MEM. A scratch prototype\n  with a short bypass for LW, LH and LHU cut ten validated CoreMark\n  iterations from 4,238,604 to 4,085,803 marker cycles. The champion's\n  register-file-to-RAM path also matters when a load feeds another address.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give MEM separate address and operand-forwarding paths. Register the\n  effective address directly from forwarded rs1 plus the immediate.\n  Feed ordinary EX results or a ready LW, LH or LHU into the existing\n  youngest-producer bypass. A halfword needs only a choice of two lanes\n  and sign fill. A byte load keeps the existing one-cycle interlock.\n  Every dependent remains held while an older data request lacks ready.\n  Only aligned loads can grant the MEM bypass.\n\n  Gowin placement option 1 reached 63.001 MHz for the prototype, which\n  combines with its measured cycle count to give 154.2 iterations/s.\n  A median above 62.48 MHz would clear the tournament threshold.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add a 32-bit effective_addr field to ex_mem_t immediately after alu_result.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture rs1 plus in.imm in effective_addr alongside write_data on EX/MEM advance. Hold both with the access controls through dmem stalls.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use effective_addr for the bus address, alignment, masks, load lanes\n      and aligned RVFI address. Export the post-trap reg_write and a 32-bit\n      MEM bypass. For a word, pass dmem_rdata. For a halfword, form the low\n      16 bits by masking and ORing the selected half. Form the upper half\n      from the selected sign bit gated by mem_sext. OR these contributions\n      with the ALU result gated by \"'!mem_read. WB retains its existing load\n      extraction for all widths.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect the MEM bypass to fwd_ex_mem and its post-trap write enable\n      to forward_unit. Classify only byte loads and multiplies as WB-only\n      producers for hazard_unit. Its existing valid and nonzero-rd checks\n      and its dmem stall freeze govern issue.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r5s0.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(146.18*1.046*4085803/1e7)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
