{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_100", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r5s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-001-r5s0\ntitle: Bypass LW, LH, LHU and LBU results directly from MEM into EX\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion, a dependent instruction waits for WB even when MEM\n  already has the load data. Ten CoreMark iterations take 4,238,604 marker\n  cycles. Forwarding LW, LH, LHU and LBU removes 202,756 cycles. Extending\n  the bypass to signed LB saved only another 1,536 cycles in simulation\n  and put a four-lane sign selection on the path to the high operand bits.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a load-data input to each EX operand mux. For LW, LH, LHU and LBU,\n  the consumer can issue immediately after the load and take its value\n  from the bus on the accepting MEM edge. Parallel byte-lane masks format\n  the value. A separate registered effective address keeps the general\n  EX result mux off the path back to RAM when a load supplies an address.\n  Signed LB and all four multiplies keep their WB interlock.\n\n  A scratch prototype on the champion passed the canonical CoreMark UART\n  and CRC checks in 4,035,848 marker cycles with both buses stalled. Gowin\n  placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 62.043, 64.147 and 64.147 MHz.\n  The median yields 158.94 iterations/s, 8.73% above 146.18. The required\n  median at this cycle count is just over 61.71 MHz. All eight RVFI trace\n  comparisons passed across selftest and three random programs, each with\n  and without bus stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Add a 32-bit effective_addr immediately after alu_result in ex_mem_t.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture forwarded rs1 plus in.imm in effective_addr on every EX/MEM\n      advance and hold it with the memory request during a stall. Add\n      mem_value and mem_load inputs. Form each operand as the OR of four\n      masked sources. Select 0 grants the saved ID/EX operand, select 2\n      grants WB, and select 1 grants either mem_value when mem_load is\n      set or fwd_ex_mem otherwise. Keep the registered ALU result on its\n      own input so a late load value traverses one forwarding mux.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive the data address, alignment, byte masks, load lanes and aligned\n      RVFI address from effective_addr. Export ctrl_with_trap.reg_write as\n      ex_write so a misaligned load cannot forward over an older writer.\n      Build a dedicated mem_bypass from dmem_rdata and the registered MEM\n      controls. Decode read enables for a word, either halfword, and each\n      byte lane. In bits 7:0 OR the enabled byte slices from all four\n      lanes, folding the word and halfword enables into those lane masks.\n      In bits 15:8 select bus bits 15:8 for LW or the low halfword, or\n      31:24 for the high halfword. In bits 31:16 OR the word's upper\n      half with the replicated selected halfword sign gated by mem_sext.\n      WB uses its existing complete load formatter, including signed LB.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire mem_bypass to EX mem_value, ex_mem_w.ctrl.mem_read to mem_load,\n      and ex_write to the EX/MEM write-enable input of forward_unit.\n      Qualify id_ex_wb_only with ID/EX valid and either is_mul(alu_op)\n      or a signed byte load (mem_read, mem_sext, mem_width zero). The\n      existing dmem stall holds the load and consumer until acceptance.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive retirements for LW, LH, LHU and LBU feeding both\n      sources of ADD, across all legal lane offsets with sign bits set.\n      Check one bubble and sign extension for LB. Exercise a stalled\n      pointer load feeding another load and then a store. Check that a\n      misaligned load to the same rd as an older writer traps and its\n      consumer gets the older value.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport jsonschema,json,yaml\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r5s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert all((Path('cores/bench')/c['file']).is_file() for c in d['changes'])\nprint(p, 'validated')\nPY\ntail -n 4 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/r5-verify/pipeline.log\"\ntail -n 2 \"$TMPDIR/r5-lbu-flat/formal.log\"'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
