 the immediate.\n  Register those controls and the full effective address at EX/MEM. In MEM,\n  select bytes and the extension sign in parallel from the raw bus word.\n  Give this formatted value its own input to each EX operand mux. This puts\n  lane decoding before the memory response and allows an accepting load and\n  its consumer to\n…[1307 of 4379 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bb337d301fa45e3c]…\n registered selects for LW, LH, LHU, LB and LBU. Supply that result\n      to both MEM/WB and the EX bypass. Export the write permission after\n      misalignment checking so a trapping load cannot shadow an older writer.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect the MEM load value and write permission to EX forwarding.\n      Reserve the existing WB-only use interlock for multiplies. Keep the\n      dmem hold on both the load and its consumer until the bus accepts.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      In predicted_load_and_multiply_consumers, require a one-cycle\n      retirement gap for LW to MUL and a two-cycle gap for MUL to ADD,\n      including when IF issues the cached successor. Check adjacent\n      ready-bus retirements for each load width, sign and\n      legal lane, including loads feeding another address, a branch and store\n      data. Vary read data during a multi-cycle hold. Check a misaligned\n      load sharing rd with an older writer and retain multiply-use coverage.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
