{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r7s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-001-r7s0\ntitle: Resolve five quotient bits per round with mixed radix-4 and radix-8 digits\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Both the champion's 64.063 MHz placement and its 66.043 MHz median\n  placement run through three serial divider digits. The median placement\n  reports a 97-cell path starting at quotient_q[34]. At 3,207,017 marker\n  cycles, beating the champion by 4.6% requires just over 69.08 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup. Their unsigned quotient\n  and remainder depend only on whether the divisor magnitude is 0, 1,\n  2, 3 or larger. Seed the quotient shift register with the remaining\n  30 dividend bits followed by these two quotient bits. Register 3D, 5D\n  and 7D during setup using 2D+D, 4D+D and 8D-D. Shifts supply the\n  other multiples.\n  \n  Each of six rounds resolves one radix-4 digit followed by one radix-8\n  digit. For radix 8 bring down three bits and test D through 7D in\n  parallel. The borrow flags select the largest multiple that fits and\n  the corresponding residual. This reduces the full-width feedback chain\n  from three serial subtract/select stages to two at the original latency.\n  A prototype measured 67.594 MHz on placement option 1. Timing there\n  moved to the predicted load word feeding the fetch occupancy update.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement the two-bit setup and six five-bit rounds with a 32-bit\n      quotient shift register. Use 35-bit operands and a 36-bit unsigned\n      difference for radix-8 trials, with 34-bit operands for radix 4.\n      Retain the existing sign corrections, held response and ALTOPS\n      handshake. For divisor zero set the two setup quotient bits to 11\n      and retain the dividend prefix as the first remainder.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend unsigned quotient and remainder vectors to k*D plus or minus\n      one for k from 4 through 7, including equality. Check all four\n      initial dividend bit pairs against divisor magnitudes 0 through 4.\n      Retain the signed reference vectors and seven-clock response checks.\nYAML\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
