{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'r7' in d['id']:\n  for k,v in d.items():\n   print(k,str(v)[:7900])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261123-001-r7s0\ntitle Resolve five quotient bits per round with mixed radix-4 and radix-8 digits\ncategory micro_opt\nmotivation Both the champion's 64.063 MHz placement and its 66.043 MHz median\nplacement run through three serial divider digits. The median placement\nreports a 97-cell path starting at quotient_q[34]. At 3,207,017 marker\ncycles, beating the champion by 4.6% requires just over 69.08 MHz.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': \"Both the champion's 64.063 MHz placement and its 66.043 MHz median\\nplacement run through three serial divider digits. The median placement\\nreports a 97-cell path starting at quotient_q[34]. At 3,207,017 marker\\ncycles, beating the champion by 4.6% requires just over 69.08 MHz.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup. Their unsigned quotient\\nand remainder depend only on whether the divisor magnitude is 0, 1,\\n2, 3 or larger. Seed the quotient shift register with the remaining\\n30 dividend bits followed by these two quotient bits. Register 3D, 5D\\nand 7D during setup using 2D+D, 4D+D and 8D-D. Shifts supply the\\nother multiples.\\n\\nEach of six rounds resolves one radix-4 digit followed by one radix-8\\ndigit. For radix 8 bring down three bits and test D through 7D in\\nparallel. The borrow flags select the largest multiple that fits and\\nthe corresponding residual. For radix 4 select with a balanced borrow\\ntree. For radix 8 mask each residual by its winning interval and OR\\nthe eight masked words. Encode the quotient bits from the borrow flags\\nin parallel. This reduces the full-width feedback chain from three\\nserial subtract/select stages to two at the original latency.\\n\\nThe prototype passed the extended ALU vectors and matched the ISS on\\nselftest and all three random traces with both buses stalled. It completed\\nten CRC-validated iterations in 3,207,017 marker cycles. Gowin measured\\n66.252, 69.004 and 69.004 MHz, giving 215.17 iterations/s. The 4.48%\\ngain falls just short of the 4.6% replacement threshold. The median\\nplacement's worst path now ru\n…[18062 of 21134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2b9ecdcaed65fa48]…\na dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.'}]\noutcome regression\nfitness 215.54\ndelta_pct 4.67\nvs_baseline 1678.38\nfmax_mhz 67.376\nipc_coremark 3e-06\ncycles 3125942\niterations 10\nlut4 5773\nff 1499\nseeds [64.983, 67.376, 67.376]\nperturbations [[0, 64.983, 12], [1, 67.376, 13], [2, 67.376, 13]]\nlutram 144\nbsram 9\ndsp 6\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/occupied_496_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.389, 'arrival_ns': 20.683, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nlogic_levels 12\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-23T01:32:41.327344Z\nslot 2\nround_id 7\nlesson - 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-003-r7s2 (regression, +4.67%): Forwarding preformatted byte and halfword loads with a registered one-hot bank select saved 81,075 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but the path from the fetch successor BRAM to its occupancy bits limited median Fmax to 67.376 MHz versus the round winner’s 70.620 MHz.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
