{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-001-r8s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-001-r8s0\ntitle: Form dependent load results with asymmetric block RAM read ports\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion interlocks every immediate byte- or halfword-load consumer.\n  The previous four-bank implementation recovered 81,075 marker cycles but\n  reached 67.376 MHz. Selecting bytes and their extension inside a synchronous\n  RAM read can preserve this cycle saving while taking the barrel shifter,\n  sign fanout and bank-selection tree off the consumer's EX operand path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Reorganize the existing 256-row verified word table so a producer selects\n  the format while addressing the RAMs. Each accepted fill writes all byte\n  lanes of the source word and their precomputed sign extensions together.\n  Each narrow read port returns exactly the fragment required at its position\n  in the 32-bit result. Concatenate the three registered outputs directly\n  into the existing speculative load bypass.\n\n  Use an 8-bit low port with four choices per row. Use an 8-bit middle port\n  with eight choices per row: byte 1, byte 3, zero, zero, then the four\n  byte-sign masks. Use a 16-bit upper port with eight choices per row:\n  the raw upper half, three zeros and the four replicated sign bits. Use the\n  exact low two address bits for the byte lane. For signed halfwords the sign\n  comes from byte 1 or byte 3. A word read selects byte 0, byte 1 and the\n  upper half. Infer the asymmetric ports with one indexed synchronous read\n  and parallel writes to constant subindices of the same word row.\n\n  Full-address, occupancy, alignment and read/write-collision checks in MEM\n  authorize consumption. A failed dependent load follows the existing hold,\n  bubble and WB replay protocol. The raw word still supplies RVFI. Keep the\n  multiply-use interlock and the verified-hit behavior under bus stalls.\n\n  A scratch prototype ran ten CRC-validated iterations in 3,125,942 cycles\n  and matched the ISS on eight retirement traces. Gowin placement 1 reached\n  70.609 MHz. At this cycle count a median above 72.001 MHz would clear the\n  tournament threshold. The control path from tag verification to a held\n  operand is the remaining timing risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the three asymmetric reads to the existing read/write schedule.\n      Broadcast each accepted full-word installation to the format memories,\n      hold all read outputs with the candidate, invalidate on narrow stores,\n      and retain the authoritative raw word and address check.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive a two-bit lane sum from the forwarded base and displacement\n      alongside the existing split word index. Feed the formatted result\n      through the existing load bypass on either source.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the EX lane, decoded width and sign mode to the lookup ports.\n      Restrict the proactive WB-only interlock to multiplies and keep replay\n      qualified by a dependent load and the MEM verification result.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Require adjacent retirements on the four warm subword hits in\n      load_table_stores_and_subwords. Keep the exact miss gaps, raw RVFI\n      words, masks and transaction counts. Exercise all legal lanes with\n      sign-bit transitions, a tag alias, and a dependent branch on a miss.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=next(Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses').glob('*.yaml'))\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())); print('valid',220.20*1.046*3125942/1e7)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
