{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r7s2','r5s0','r6s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-001-r5s0 Add a load-data input to each EX operand mux. For LW, LH, LHU and LBU,\nthe consumer can issue immediately after the load and take its value\nfrom the bus on the accepting MEM edge. Parallel byte-lane masks format\nthe value. A separate registered effective address keeps the general\nEX result mux off the path back to RAM when a load supplies an address.\nSigned LB and all four multiplies keep their WB interlock.\n\nA scratch prototype on the champion passed the canonical CoreMark UART\nand CRC checks in 4,035,848 marker cycles with both buses stalled. Gowin\nplacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 62.043, 64.147 and 64.147 MHz.\nThe median yields 158.94 iterations/s, 8.73% above 146.18. At this\ncycle count 61.71 MHz clears the acceptance margin. Placement 0 used\n3,268 LUT4s and 676 flip-flops. All 53 single-retire ALTOPS checks,\neight RVFI trace comparisons and 92 cocotb tests passed.\n\nhyp-20261123-001-r6s0 Let a dependent instruction enter EX immediately after any legal load.\nCompute the load format controls in the producer's EX cycle from its\nwidth, signedness and the low two bits of the sum of forwarded rs1 and\nthe immediate.\nRegister those controls and the full effective address at EX/MEM. In MEM,\nselect bytes and the extension sign in parallel from the raw bus word.\nGive this formatted value its own input to each EX operand mux. This puts\nlane decoding before the memory response and allows an accepting load and\nits consumer to advance on the same edge. Consecutive pointer loads are\na timing stress case because a returned pointer feeds the next address.\n\nA scratch prototype passed the canonical CoreMark UART and CRC checks in\n3,260,731 bracketed cycles, saving 203,262 cycles (5.87%) with both\nrandom stall generators active. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2\nreached 56.085, 62.537 and 62.537 MHz. The median gives 191.79\niterations/s, 10.62% above the champion. At that cycle count,\n59.14 MHz clears the acceptance margin.\nPlacement zero used 4,133 logic cells and 1,211 FFs. The prototype\npassed all 53\n…[1622 of 4694 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6343e1b8d6d40984]…\nold a dependent consumer through backpressure, bubble it once on\ncompletion, and retry from WB. Gate redirect, training, division and\nwrites on successful advance. Preserve collision suppression, reset\ninvalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store invalidation.\nKeep the WB-only multiply interlock.\n\nA single-bank control prototype passed the canonical UART and five CRC checks\nin 3,125,942 marker cycles, saving 81,075 cycles over the champion.\nGowin measured 62.721, 65.795 and 65.795 MHz. The median gives\n210.48 iterations/s, a 2.2% gain. At that cycle count the tournament\nrequires more than 67.334 MHz. The longest median-placement path\nended at the shared EX/MEM result register through the predictor read\nand format logic. All 30 directed pipeline cases passed on the control prototype. The proposed four-bank layout targets 68.25 MHz,\nwhich would give 218.33 iterations/s at the measured cycle count.\nIts post-route clock and the delay of the consumer mux remain unmeasured.\n\nMon Nov 23 03:29:02 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
