{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-002-r10s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-002-r10s1\ntitle: Complete radix-16 division across EX and MEM\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  In the champion's 78.376 MHz placement, the divider feedback path arrives\n  within 0.002 ns of the worst setup path. Each clock first selects a radix-4\n  remainder and then feeds that result to a radix-8 trial. Earlier CoreMark\n  tracing found zero divides between the timing markers, so a later bypass\n  for divide results costs no cycles in that window.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split DIV/REM completion across EX and MEM. At request acceptance capture\n  operand magnitudes, signs and operation. In setup, divide the top four\n  dividend bits by the divisor using a four-bit lookup for divisors 1 to 15.\n  A larger divisor leaves the prefix as remainder. For zero, emit digit 15\n  and retain the prefix. In parallel register the odd divisor multiples up\n  to 15D. Shifts supply all the even multiples.\n\n  Execute six registered radix-16 rounds. Each round appends four dividend\n  bits to the remainder and subtracts all fifteen nonzero multiples in\n  parallel, using 36-bit multiples and a separate borrow bit. Select the\n  largest fitting multiple and its residual. During the response cycle,\n  reuse the same trials on the stable state for the eighth and final digit.\n  Latch the selected quotient or remainder magnitude and its negate flag on\n  transfer. MEM restores the sign and writes the result to MEM/WB. Interlock\n  adjacent divide consumers like multiply consumers so they read the final\n  signed result. Preserve response backpressure, reset cancellation, saved\n  RVFI operands and the ALTOPS result with the same handshake.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten CRC-validated CoreMark iterations in\n  3,140,795 marker cycles at a median 79.413 MHz. That is 252.84 iterations/s,\n  a 1.3% gain. The 4.6% replacement threshold at this cycle count requires\n  more than 81.98 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Implement shared radix-16 trials, prefix setup and response-cycle final digit. Supply magnitude and sign separately to the pipeline and retain the signed standalone ALU result.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the response sign with the EX/MEM magnitude.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the unsigned divide result and sign on a verified response transfer, alongside the saved instruction and its original operands.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Apply the quotient or remainder sign before writing the MEM/WB result.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Interlock consumers of DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU destinations until WB can forward the signed value.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Sweep quotient digits 0 through 15 on both sides of each trial boundary, including divisors whose high multiples exceed 32 bits and responses held under backpressure.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nprint(79.413e6*10/3140795,249.54*1.046*3140795/1.e7)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
