ons/s,\n  a 1.3% gain. The 4.6% replacement threshold at this cycle count requires\n  more than 81.98 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Implement shared radix-16 trials, prefix setup and response-cycle final digit. Supply magnitude and sign separately to the pipeline and retain the signed standalone ALU result.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the response sign with the EX/MEM magnitude.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the unsigned divide result and sign on a verified response transfer, alongside the saved instruction and its original operands.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Apply the quotient or remainder sign before writing the MEM/WB result.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Interlock consumers of DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU destinations until WB can forward the signed value.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Sweep quotient digits 0 through 15 on both sides of each trial boundary, including divisors whose high multiples exceed 32 bits and responses held under backpressure.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nprint(79.413e6*10/3140795,249.54*1.046*3140795/1.e7)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"252.84362717082777 81.98066675778\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
