{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r.get('round_id') in (10,11) and r.get('slot') in (0,1,2):\n  for k in ['id','hypothesis','lut4','ff','lutram','bsram','dsp','cycles']: print(k,r.get(k))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261123-001-r10s0\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The verified load table puts two partial address adders, a 256-row data\\nlookup and word-versus-subword selection between a forwarded base and the\\nnext predicted-value register. Its 256-bit occupied vector also needs a\\nfull indexed read in that cycle. Ten CoreMark iterations take 3,140,795\\nmarker cycles. At that count the 4.6 percent margin requires 81.981 MHz.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Pipeline the existing table lookup by one bank-select bit without adding\\na load-use cycle. Split the 256 payload rows into two 128-row distributed\\nRAM banks. Read both with lookup_index[6:0]. At EX/MEM capture each bank's\\nraw word, tag, signature and already selected word or extended subword.\\nCapture lookup_index[7] with them. At each dependent EX operand form two\\nenables from its existing speculative-load enable and that registered\\nbank bit. OR the two masked candidates into the existing forwarding mux.\\nThis places the bank decision in parallel with bypass selection. MEM uses\\nthe same bank bit for verification, raw RVFI data and the WB candidate.\\n\\nStage the occupancy lookup at the same edge. Read a 16-bit group mask\\nwith index[7:4] and capture it alongside its initialized flag and index.\\nUse index[3:0] for the final bit select in MEM. Reset clears the 16 group\\nflags and invalidates the candidate. Start the first update to each group\\nfrom zero, set the target bit on install, and clear it on an accepted\\nnarrow store. Suppress a same-row read/write collision and hold both\\nbanks, their selects and their validity sample together during bus stalls.\\nKeep full-address, alignment and format checks and the existing replay\\nconditions so a wrong partial sum cannot authorize a bypass.\\n\\nThe directory-only control prototype passed the pipeline suite and the\\ncanonical CoreMark run in 3,140,795 marker cycles. Its Gowin placements\\nreached 77.475, 80.815 and 80.815 MHz, for 257.31 iterations/s. Eight of\\nthe next timing paths after the divider in the median placement ran from\\nW\n…[15642 of 18714 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19fab7848ed2a458]…\n carry-dependent XOR mask in ID/EX.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the row from the low ten bits of the register-file base plus displacement, and its XOR mask, on ID advance.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Precompute the WB row using the consumer displacement and the producer estimate. Hold it with the WB data.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive lookup_index with the one-hot OR of the four source-specific row predictions.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the eight-bit WB row to EX and select the incoming or held consumer displacement for MEM.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a decode carry estimate invalidated by forwarding and a WB base estimate taken from a missed load. Update exact hit and miss expectations in load_index_discarded_carries for the new predictor. Check bus addresses, dependent replay, retirement and absence of wrong-path stores.'}]}\nlut4 7521\nff 1489\nlutram 312\nbsram 6\ndsp 6\ncycles 3134538\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
