{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r.get('round_id') in (7,8,9) and r.get('slot') in (0,2):\n  print(r.get('id'),r.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-001-r7s0 Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup. Their unsigned quotient\nand remainder depend only on whether the divisor magnitude is 0, 1,\n2, 3 or larger. Seed the quotient shift register with the remaining\n30 dividend bits followed by these two quotient bits. Register 3D, 5D\nand 7D during setup using 2D+D, 4D+D and 8D-D. Shifts supply the\nother multiples.\n\nEach of six rounds resolves one radix-4 digit followed by one radix-8\ndigit. For radix 8 bring down three bits and test D through 7D in\nparallel. The borrow flags select the largest multiple that fits and\nthe corresponding residual. For radix 4 select with a balanced borrow\ntree. For radix 8 mask each residual by its winning interval and OR\nthe eight masked words. Encode the quotient bits from the borrow flags\nin parallel. This reduces the full-width feedback chain from three\nserial subtract/select stages to two at the original latency.\n\nThe prototype passed the extended ALU vectors and matched the ISS on\nselftest and all three random traces with both buses stalled. It completed\nten CRC-validated iterations in 3,207,017 marker cycles. Gowin measured\n66.252, 69.004 and 69.004 MHz, giving 215.17 iterations/s. The 4.48%\ngain falls just short of the 4.6% replacement threshold. The median\nplacement's worst path now runs from the word table through the EX ALU.\n\nhyp-20261123-003-r7s2 Split a 256-word load-value predictor into four 64-row distributed\nRAM banks. As in the champion, assemble the predicted word index from\nindependent sums of base and displacement bits [9:5] and [4:2].\nUse index[5:0] to read all four banks in the producer's EX cycle.\nAdd the low two address bits exactly. Format each candidate in parallel\nfor the producer's width, lane and sign mode. At EX/MEM capture the four\nvalue candidates, a one-hot selection for index[7:6], and the ordinary\ninteger result separately. This moves the last two bits of row selection\nacross the register and removes the ALU-versus-load mux from the\npredictor read path.\n\nAt each consuming EX source, q\n…[8266 of 11338 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6fbc105cb79c8b58]…\nof MMIO.\n\nPick the raw field for LW and the formatted field for narrow loads using\nthe producer's registered width. Feed that candidate directly to a dependent\nEX operand. In parallel MEM verifies the tag and index, alignment and, for\nnarrow loads, the signature. On success the identical candidate drives WB.\nOn a signature miss the verified raw word can still complete the load\ninternally. Hold and retry an actual dependent consumer from WB on either\nkind of miss, suppressing its redirects, training and side effects until\nit can advance. Raw data and masks continue to supply RVFI. Keep the\nspeculative load source as a parallel one-hot term with the three ordinary\nforwarding sources so the register-file path through EX avoids the existing\nfinal load-select mux.\n\nCount signature hits specifically at adjacent dependent subword uses in\nthe marker window. Measure marker cycles and median Gowin Fmax together.\nAt 3.15 million cycles the design needs just over 76.2 MHz to clear the\n4.6 percent replacement threshold.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
