\n  For D >= 2048, the quotient fits in 21 bits. Consume three dividend bits\n  per round for D < 2^18, two for 2^18 <= D < 2^25, and one above that\n  boundary including equality. In setup seed the remainder with N >> (7*s)\n  for the selected digit width s. This prefix is strictly below D. Register\n  the needed divisor mu\n…[1074 of 4146 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c9001511fa48e00c]…\nreciprocal ROM, limb-product schedule and seven-trial recurrence behind the existing divider handshake. Supply separate completion terms for MEM and the exact standalone response.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the registered divide completion fields and their selection through EX/MEM.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Capture divider completion separately on an accepted response and remove its contribution to the fast ALU bypass. Retain issue and replay qualification.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Select the divide completion and apply its registered sign before MEM/WB writeback.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Exercise both sides of 2048, 2^18 and 2^25, exact multiples and their neighbors, low-product wraparound, maximum numerators, sign extremes and held responses.\ntotal 20\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody   nogroup  4096 Nov 23 08:39 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody   nogroup  4096 Nov 23 08:35 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench 3954 Nov 23 08:39 hyp-20261123-002-r13s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
