{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261123-003-r7s2','hyp-20261123-002-r6s1'):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'],r['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-002-r6s1 {'motivation': 'The champion takes 3,463,993 marker cycles for ten iterations at 60.060 MHz.\\nIts reported 23.186 ns path runs from the register file through EX to data RAM.\\nRegister-file write-through, forwarding priority and ALU operand selection\\ncan all contribute mux delay. Decode already knows the incoming source\\nindices and the destinations of all three older in-flight instructions.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Move forwarding arbitration across the ID/EX register. For each source, decode\\nselects the youngest effective writer and registers a one-hot mask that names\\nwhere its value will be in the following cycle. EX forms each operand by ORing\\nthe masked data buses. Give raw word-load data its own input so an aligned LW\\nand its immediate consumer can advance on successive clocks. Give the ALU\\ninputs their own registered masks with PC and immediate choices so those muxes\\nalso resolve in decode. Byte and halfword loads and multiplies use the existing\\nWB interlock.\\n\\nA scratch prototype on this champion completed ten iterations in 3,344,675\\nmarker cycles with all five CRCs correct. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2\\nreached 63.152, 65.278 and 65.278 MHz. The median gives 195.17 iterations/s,\\n12.57 percent above the champion. The prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 13, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Replace the EX-stage forward_unit instance with decode-time priority\\nselection for each source. Compare rs1 and rs2 to the effective EX, MEM\\nand WB writers in youngest-first order. Use five mask bits per source,\\nin ascending bit order for raw RF, saved WB, following-cycle WB,\\nfollowing-cycle EX/MEM ALU result and the returning LW bus. Give x0 a\\nzero mask. Capture current WB data, both masks and both ALU-specific\\nmasks on exactly the ID/EX advance enable. For ALU A select PC on AUIPC;\\nfor ALU B select the immediate on alu_src. Wire io_dmemRData directly\\nto the word-load input. Apply the us\n…[8739 of 11811 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a6cd28bab2d5422b]…\nfour 64-row banks in parallel, format each candidate, verify the selected row and send the accepted value or formatted bus response to WB.'}, {'file': 'rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'description': 'Use the registered bank choice and youngest-writer load match to generate bank-specific operand enables. Keep the combined load match for replay.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX lookup, four predictions and registered bank select, reserve the proactive interlock for multiply, and use the dependent-load bit and the MEM verdict to replay rejected consumers.'}, {'file': 'rtl/wb_stage.sv', 'description': 'Forward and write back the completed result selected at the MEM/WB edge.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Require adjacent retirements for a warm subword load and its consumer. Check all four banks at the same row offset with different words, every legal lane and sign boundary, raw RVFI words and masks, and a dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
