during setup using 2D+D, 4D+D and 8D-D. Shifts supply the\nother multiples.\n\nEach of six rounds resolves one radix-4 digit followed by one radix-8\ndigit. For radix 8 bring down three bits and test D through 7D in\nparallel. The borrow flags select the largest multiple that fits and\nthe corresponding residual. For radix 4 select with a balanced borrow\ntree. For radix 8 mask each residual by its winning interval and OR\nthe eight masked words. Encode the qu\n…[3187 of 6259 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5a7c51c951a81fd7]…\nso it remains available across repeated holds. Capture that shadow from the previous cycle's registered selection. Keep the full successor-PC check and live instruction priority.\n\nCapture each accepted live fill as a one-entry write pipeline carrying the predecessor index, successor PC, word, decoded target and branch flags. Commit one registered fill per clock to both BRAM and occupancy. Align the read-valid bit with the row actually read and mask same-address BRAM read/write collisions. Reset and FENCE.I must squash pending fills and candidates, including the shadow. Register the bulk occupancy clear and suppress candidate validity until it takes effect. EX still corrects the fetch PC on its existing edge. Only local registered controls should reach the table ports and the occupancy write network.\n\nA median above 73.87 MHz at the champion's cycle count would clear the acceptance gate. Check the vendor path endpoints and the bracketed cycle count separately to see whether this retiming achieves that gain.\n \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
