or training. Capture the\\npreceding index, live-fill eligibility and full 70-bit successor record.\\nCombine registered eligibility with registered acceptance for the write.\\nRepresent occupancy as 32 resettable group-valid bits and 32 masks of\\n16 rows in distributed RAM. The first fill of an invalid group writes\\na one-hot mask. Later fills OR the row bit into its current mask. If a\\nlookup reads a group being updated, forward the new mask \n…[11820 of 14892 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1360fa0031738bf9]…\nelect mux.\\n\\nCount signature hits specifically at adjacent dependent subword uses in\\nthe marker window. Measure marker cycles and median Gowin Fmax together.\\nAt 3.15 million cycles the design needs just over 76.2 MHz to clear the\\n4.6 percent replacement threshold.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Keep raw and formatted data together, train and verify the format signature, and supply the verified bypass value to WB.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Remove the subword-use interlock and qualify dependent replay with formatted-value verification.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Forward the candidate through the existing per-source one-hot network and retain the replay suppression of side effects.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise repeated and changing byte and halfword signatures, store invalidation, exact RVFI masks and values, and held or replayed consumers.'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
