{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat tools/eval/gowin.py | head -260; cat test/cosim/build.sh; cat bench/programs/Makefile; rg -n 'istall|usage|UART|json' test/cosim/main.cpp\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = [*rtl_sources(rtl_dir), worktree / STALL_GEN, worktree / bench_sv,\n             worktree / CST, worktree / SDC]\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"set_device {PART} -device_version {DEVICE_VERSION}\",\n        *(f\"add_file {f}\" for f in fi\n…[12570 of 15642 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9639ac429d12ef63]…\nv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n.PHONY: all clean\nall: bench/programs/coremark.elf bench/programs/selftest.elf $(RANDOM_ELFS)\nclean:\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n63:        std::cerr << \"usage: sim <elf> [maxcycles] [--bench] [--istall] [--dstall] [--seed N]\\n\";\n68:    // --istall: random ~22% imem-bus backpressure (VexRiscv-style).\n74:    bool istall = false;\n78:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--istall\") == 0) istall     = true;\n107:    // UART capture: writes to 0x10000000 go to stdout as characters, not dmem.\n119:        top->io_imemReady = istall ? bus_accepts_main() : 1;\n126:        //     the UART range, which is write-only. Reads from UART used to\n129:        //     UART reads flag oob and return 0.\n130:        //   - dmem write: UART range is allowed (TX); BENCH_START/STOP are\n150:            // MMIO UART at 0x10000000: capture to uart_buf, don't route to dmem\n172:                // OOB write (neither dmem nor UART). Flag so testbench reports it.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r10s1','r10s2','r8s0','r9s2','r10s0')):\n  print(r['id']); print(r['hypothesis']);print({k:r[k] for k in ['bsram','lutram','logic_levels','cycles','fitness']})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r10s1','r10s2','r8s0','r9s2','r10s0')):\n  print(r['id']); print(r['hypothesis']);print({k:r[k] for k in ['bsram','lutram','logic_levels','cycles','fitness']})\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-001-r8s0\n{'motivation': \"The champion interlocks every immediate byte- or halfword-load consumer.\\nThe previous four-bank implementation recovered 81,075 marker cycles but\\nreached 67.376 MHz. Selecting bytes and their extension inside a synchronous\\nRAM read can preserve this cycle saving while taking the barrel shifter,\\nsign fanout and bank-selection tree off the consumer's EX operand path.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Reorganize the existing 256-row verified word table so a producer selects\\nthe format while addressing the RAMs. Each accepted fill writes all byte\\nlanes of the source word and their precomputed sign extensions together.\\nEach narrow read port returns exactly the fragment required at its position\\nin the 32-bit result. Concatenate the three registered outputs directly\\ninto the existing speculative load bypass.\\n\\nUse an 8-bit low port with four choices per row. Use an 8-bit middle port\\nwhose slots 0 and 1 hold bytes 1 and 3, slots 2 and 3 hold zero, and\\nslots 4 through 7 hold the four byte-sign masks. The 16-bit upper port\\nholds the raw upper half in slot 0, zeros in slots 1 through 3 and the\\nfour replicated sign bits in slots 4 through 7. The byte lane comes from\\nthe exact low two address bits. For signed halfwords the sign\\ncomes from byte 1 or byte 3. A word read selects byte 0, byte 1 and the\\nupper half. Infer the asymmetric ports with one indexed synchronous read\\nand parallel writes to constant subindices of the same word row.\\n\\nFull-address, occupancy, alignment and read/write-collision checks in MEM\\nauthorize consumption. A failed dependent load follows the existing hold,\\nbubble and WB replay protocol. The raw word still supplies RVFI. Keep the\\nmultiply-use interlock and the verified-hit behavior under bus stalls.\\n\\nA scratch prototype ran ten CRC-validated iterations in 3,125,942 cycles\\nand matched the ISS on selftest and three random programs with ready and\\nstalled buses. All 30 directed pipeline cases passed with the new one-cycle\\nhit expectation and additional signed and unsigned lane cases. Gowin\\nplacements 0, 1 and 2 reached 68.473, 70.609 and 70.609 MHz. The median\\ngives 225.88 iterations/s, a 2.58% gain. Placement 0 used 17 of the 46\\nBSRAMs, up from 10, and 4,683 logic cells, down from 4,824. The 4.6% margin\\nrequires 72.00 MHz at this cycle count. The median placement's critical\\npath runs from the raw word/tag RAM, through load verification and replay,\\nto register-file read control.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 3, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the three asymmetric reads to the existing read/write schedule.\\nBroadcast each accepted full-word installation to the format memories,\\nhold all read outputs with the candidate, and invalidate on accepted\\nnarrow stores. Feed WB and RVFI from the verified raw word or the\\nactual bus response as in the champion.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive a two-bit lane sum from the forwarded base and displacement\\nalongside the existing split word index. Feed the formatted result\\nthrough the existing load bypass on either source.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the EX lane, decoded width and sign mode to the lookup ports.\\nRestrict the proactive WB-only interlock to multiplies and keep replay\\nqualified by a dependent load and the MEM verification result.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Require adjacent retirements on the four warm subword hits in\\nload_table_stores_and_subwords. Keep the exact miss gaps, raw RVFI\\nwords, masks and transaction counts. Exercise all legal lanes with\\nsign-bit transitions, a tag alias, and a dependent branch on a miss.\\n'}]}\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 4, in <module>\nKeyError: 'bsram'\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
