{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r11s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-003-r11s2\ntitle: Predict the load-table index from a forwarded base and an early carry estimate\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  In a repeat of the champion's 83.455 MHz Gowin placement, three of the\n  seven longest paths ran from WB read data or its result select to load-table\n  output registers. The table address currently waits for the architectural\n  WB mux, operand forwarding and two partial additions. MEM already verifies\n  the complete word address before the CPU can consume a predicted value.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the 256-row load predictor its own eight-bit estimate of the address\n  base. In ID compute an eight-bit mask from the register-file sample B and\n  the load's I-immediate D. The mask is B[9:2] XOR (B + D)[9:2], using a\n  ten-bit sum. Capture it with the load. In EX, XOR this mask with the\n  forwarded base slice to predict the row. The index is exact when the\n  relevant carries agree with ID's estimate, even if the base value changed.\n  Carries from the byte offset are included.\n  \n  For the WB forwarding case, register the predicted base bits separately\n  at MEM/WB. Take bits 9:2 of the older load's speculative bypass value or\n  the older non-load's EX/MEM ALU result, selected by mem_to_reg. Hold this\n  register with WB data on a bus stall. EX selects this slice alongside the\n  captured, EX/MEM and adjacent-load slices using the existing one-hot\n  operand enables. A bus miss, multiply or signed divide may give a poor WB\n  estimate. The estimate drives only the table read address. The normal\n  forwarded rs1 still computes the architectural effective address.\n  \n  Keep the existing indexed read, saved index, full word-address and format\n  verification, MMIO exclusion, collision rejection and replay discipline.\n  Fills and invalidations use the true address. Thus even an arbitrary\n  estimate can only turn a potential internal hit into an ordinary miss.\n  A scratch prototype completed the ten-iteration bracket in 3,135,599\n  cycles with both bus stalls and all five canonical CRCs, compared with\n  3,140,795 for the champion. At this count the replacement gate requires\n  about 87.15 MHz median. The projected gain depends primarily on timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the eight-bit predicted displacement mask in ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Form the mask from the low ten register-file and immediate bits and capture it on normal ID advance.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Register an eight-bit WB base estimate from the speculative load value or the EX/MEM ALU result, with the existing WB data hold behavior.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Select the predictor's base slice with the rs1 bypass enables and XOR the saved mask into it to drive lookup_index.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect the eight predictor-only base bits from MEM to EX.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise a decode carry estimate invalidated by forwarding and a WB base estimate taken from a missed load. Check the actual bus address, dependent replay, retirement and absence of wrong-path stores.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r11s2.yaml')\nr=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()); jsonschema.validate(r,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(r['id'],r['category'],round(265.71*1.046*3135599/1e7,3))\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
