cement options. The median gives 13.08 iterations/s, 7.9% above\\nthe 12.12 baseline, at a cost of 471 additional LUT4s. The prototype passed\\nall 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Predict the successor of each accepted instruction in the combined IF/ID\\nstage. For a legal conditional branch, evaluate its funct3 comparison on\\nthe two current register-file read values. Predict the PC-relative target\\non true and PC+4 on false. For JAL use the J target\n…[55388 of 58460 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6c95b23afdc2af8b]…\nkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry the decoded row and eight-bit carry-dependent XOR mask in ID/EX.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the row from the low ten bits of the register-file base plus displacement, and its XOR mask, on ID advance.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Precompute the WB row using the consumer displacement and the producer estimate. Hold it with the WB data.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive lookup_index with the one-hot OR of the four source-specific row predictions.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the eight-bit WB row to EX and select the incoming or held consumer displacement for MEM.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a decode carry estimate invalidated by forwarding and a WB base estimate taken from a missed load. Update exact hit and miss expectations in load_index_discarded_carries for the new predictor. Check bus addresses, dependent replay, retirement and absence of wrong-path stores.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
