{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r7s2','r8s0','r9s2','r11s2')):\n  print(r['id'],r['motivation'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],sep='\\\\n')\nPY\nsed -n '1,240p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-003-r7s2\nThe champion still interlocks every immediate consumer of LB, LBU, LH\nand LHU. Its ten-iteration CoreMark bracket contained 83,985 subword\nload-use holds with ID free to advance. The load's width, sign mode\nand byte lane are already available in EX. Preparing the value there\nlets a dependent instruction use the same registered operand path as\nan integer addition.\n\nSplit a 256-word load-value predictor into four 64-row distributed\nRAM banks. As in the champion, assemble the predicted word index from\nindependent sums of base and displacement bits [9:5] and [4:2].\nUse index[5:0] to read all four banks in the producer's EX cycle.\nAdd the low two address bits exactly. Format each candidate in parallel\nfor the producer's width, lane and sign mode. At EX/MEM capture the four\nvalue candidates, a one-hot selection for index[7:6], and the ordinary\ninteger result separately. This moves the last two bits of row selection\nacross the register and removes the ALU-versus-load mux from the\npredictor read path.\n\nAt each consuming EX source, qualify the four bank enables with the\nyoungest-writer load-forwarding enable. OR the masked bank outputs\ndirectly with the masked captured, WB and ordinary EX/MEM operands.\nThus choosing the bank and choosing the bypass source need only one\ndata selection network. MEM can select the same bank in parallel for WB.\nFull SWs and accepted read fills update just the addressed bank.\n\nRegister the matching raw word, tag, predicted index and collision-qualified\noccupancy with the producer. At MEM verify alignment and the entire\nRAM word address, including the zero upper bits. On a verified hit,\nuse the registered prediction for WB and the raw word for RVFI.\nA miss uses the actual bus word, exact lane and architectural format.\nHold a dependent consumer through backpressure, bubble it once on\ncompletion, and retry from WB. Gate redirect, training, division and\nwrites on successful advance. Preserve collision suppression, reset\ninvalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store \n…[16639 of 19711 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:df8456e36d9436ac]…\n:\n            print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: FAILED ({r.get('reason')})\")\n            continue\n        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n              f\"logic {r['logic']}, registers {r['regs']}, LUT-RAM {r['lutram']}, BSRAM {r['bsram']}, DSP {r['dsp']}\")\n        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n        for i, p in enumerate(critical_paths(tr.read_text(errors=\"replace\"), a.paths), 1):\n            print(f\"  path {i}: {p['arrival_ns']} ns, {p['logic_cells']} cells, {p['from']} -> {p['to']}\")\n            print(f\"          through: {' > '.join(p['modules'])}\")\n        print(f\"  full report: {tr}\")\n    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
