{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(s)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r1s2','r3s2','r4s2','r5s2','r10s1','r10s2','r12s2')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'],r['critical_path'][:380] if isinstance(r['critical_path'],str) else str(r['critical_path'])[:380])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 {'motivation': 'The baseline fetches PC+4 after every instruction. IF and ID share a cycle,\\nso each aligned taken branch or jump squashes one fetch slot when EX redirects.\\nBoth source registers are already read in that cycle, including same-cycle WB\\nbypass. When these values are current, they give the exact branch direction\\nor indirect jump target. Restricting prediction to those signals keeps the\\npredictor off the combinational EX ALU result path.\\n\\nA scratch RTL prototype ran the ten-iteration CoreMark timing bracket in\\n4,163,829 cycles with both stall generators active, down from 4,491,485.\\nAll five CRCs matched. Gowin reported 5.128, 5.447 and 5.447 MHz across its\\nthree placement options. The median gives 13.08 iterations/s, 7.9% above\\nthe 12.12 baseline, at a cost of 471 additional LUT4s. The prototype passed\\nall 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal checks.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Predict the successor of each accepted instruction in the combined IF/ID\\nstage. For a legal conditional branch, evaluate its funct3 comparison on\\nthe two current register-file read values. Predict the PC-relative target\\non true and PC+4 on false. For JAL use the J target, and for legal JALR\\nuse (rs1_read + I-immediate) with bit zero cleared. Select the target only\\nif it is word-aligned and below 0x00100000. Otherwise predict PC+4.\\nA pending register write can make a prediction stale, so EX resolves every\\ntransfer using its forwarded operands, alignment checks and trap rules.\\n\\nWhen a valid control transfer advances through EX, compare its resolved\\nsuccessor against the current registered fetch PC. That PC is the prediction\\nselected at the edge that admitted this instruction to ID/EX. A mismatch\\nredirects to the resolved successor and kills the younger instruction.\\nA match lets ID accept the current fetch without a control bubble. Hold\\nboth the PC and ID/EX during a data-memory freeze. On release, correction\\ntakes priority even when imemReady is low. A load-use bubble or unready\\ninstruction bus m\n…[23510 of 26582 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f75ffee2da036261]…\nt of changing row orientation together with median\\nGowin Fmax.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Store the tagged rotated word and offset, derive both the predicted operand and MEM raw word from it, and refresh on a verified word with a mismatched lane.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Route the producer's load width and signedness alongside the existing speculative row index so MEM can register its fixed-slice bypass candidate.\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise all four byte orientations, alternating signedness, halfword and word promotion, a same-row collision, and a dependent branch during an external stall. Check load masks, raw words, register results and retirement PCs.'}]} {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_26_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.452, 'arrival_ns': 17.746, 'logic_cells': 42, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
