{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r13s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-003-r13s2\ntitle: Prepare each branch's next direction when its outcome resolves\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion missed 54,467 of 529,588 advancing conditional branches\n  during the ten-iteration bracket. Replaying the same outcomes in\n  program order with eight bits of local history and 1,024 shared two-bit\n  counters produced 29,934 misses in a trace model with immediate training.\n  Round 10 found that even a small improvement in direction accuracy could\n  be lost on the fetch timing path. A branch can prepare its next prediction\n  when its previous instance resolves, leaving one direction bit to read\n  when fetch revisits its PC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Index a 1,024-bit direction array with PC[11:2]. Use its bit for either\n  a live or verified cached conditional branch, with the existing exact\n  direct target and alignment and range checks. When a legal branch\n  advances from EX, register its ten-bit PC index and the direction IF\n  actually applied. XOR this saved bit with the matching registered EX\n  correction to recover the aligned taken outcome.\n  \n  Read that PC's eight-bit local history H in the training pipeline, shift\n  in the outcome to form Hnew, and write Hnew back. Register two ten-bit\n  pattern indices, PC[11:2] XOR (H << 2) and PC[11:2] XOR (Hnew << 2).\n  Update the saturating counter at the old index. Publish the sign bit of\n  the counter at the new index in the PC's fast direction array. If the\n  indices coincide, publish the just-trained MSB. Initialize history and\n  direction to zero and counters to weakly not taken. The update pipeline\n  accepts one resolution per clock. A rapid revisit can see an older hint\n  and EX still recovers on a mismatch.\n  \n  The only fetch-side predictor read is the direction bit. Holds, replays\n  and invalid slots cannot produce a training event. Gate pending writes\n  on reset. Count misses and cycles between the MMIO markers and use the\n  median of Gowin's three placement options to test the throughput claim.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Replace the fetch counter read and pending-write bypass with the fast direction array. Pipeline history lookup, counter training and publication of the next hint.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Route the complete resolving PC index and applied fetch direction to IF with the existing advancing-branch training pulse.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Export the branch PC index and applied direction and remove the old counter update. Keep EX recovery and training eligibility tied to verified advance.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Remove the fetched counter snapshot from the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Retain the applied direction with the instruction for recovery and drop the counter snapshot.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise periodic branch outcomes, consecutive resolutions, two PCs sharing a pattern counter and a held or replayed branch. Verify retirement PCs and wrong-path store suppression.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r13s2.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(f.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Validated',f)\nPY\ndate -u +%T\nhead -c 400 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/predictor.xIefk6/packed.first\"\nhead -c 660 \"$TMPDIR/predictor.xIefk6/ahead.result\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
