decode issue a word saved during a load-use or data-memory stall even with `imem_ready` low, cutting timed CoreMark cycles by 3.1% versus 6.4% for direct-branch prediction at a similar Fmax.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261\n…[8734 of 11806 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:aefd51a9a92b238e]…\ngn extension to `predicted_value` cut median Fmax from 83.455 to 82.178 MHz.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-001-r13s0 (regression, +0.99%): Replacing 15 radix-16 trial subtractors with a 512-row quadratic reciprocal estimate and one conditional correction exposed the successor BRAM path to `predicted_pc_q`, which limited prototype placement 1 to 86.628 MHz against the 87.29 MHz needed at the same timed CoreMark cycle count.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-002-r13s1 (improvement, +6.31%): Handling divisor magnitudes 2–2047 with a reciprocal ROM and two multipliers left at most 21 quotient bits for larger divisors, cutting the clock-limiting bank from 15 trial subtractors to seven totaling 170 data bits.\n- 2026-11-23 hyp-20261123-003-r13s2 (regression, +0.53%): Precomputing one direction bit per PC from eight bits of local history cut CoreMark branch misses by 45.5% but timed cycles by only 0.78%, while the path from `saved_raw` to `direct_q` limited median Fmax to 83.242 MHz against the 86.62 MHz needed for replacement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
