{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files cores/bench/test && python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=[json.loads(x) for x in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')][-2];print({k:r[k] for k in ['fmax_mhz','cycles','fitness','seeds','perturbations','lut4','ff','lutram','bsram','dsp']});print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_multiplier.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n{'fmax_mhz': 88.718, 'cycles': 3140795, 'fitness': 282.47, 'seeds': [81.524, 88.718, 88.718], 'perturbations': [[0, 81.524, 9], [1, 88.718, 8], [2, 88.718, 8]], 'lut4': 7031, 'ff': 1414, 'lutram': 312, 'bsram': 10, 'dsp': 7}\nSplit unsigned magnitude division at D = 2048. For 2 <= D < 2048, read\nM = floor(2^32 / D) from a synchronous 2048-by-32 constant ROM in setup.\nForm q0 = high32(N * M). Since N < 2^32, truncating the reciprocal loses\nless than one quotient unit. Thus q0 is exact or one low, and the residual\nr0 = N - q0*D lies in [0, 2D). It fits in 12 bits. Compute it by subtracting\nthe low 12 product bits from N[11:0] modulo 4096. If r0 >= D, increment\nq0 and subtract D from r0. Bypass D=1 with (N, 0) and D=0 with\n(0xffffffff, N), using the existing RV32M sign rules.\n\nUse two registered unsigned 16-by-16 multipliers for the small-divisor\npath. In rounds one and two form the four limb products of N and M. In\nround three sum the middle limbs and separately sum the high terms. In\nround four add the middle carry into the high sum to obtain q0. Reuse a\nmultiplier for q0[11:0] * D[10:0] in round five and register the residual\nin round six. The response cycle handles the single correction. Generate\nROM constants at elaboration with a 64-bit numerator.\n\nFor D >= 2048, the quotient fits in 21 bits. Consume three dividend bits\nper round for D < 2^18, two for 2^18 <= D < 2^25, and one above that\nboundary including equality. In setup seed the remainder with N >> (7*s)\nfor the selected digit width s. This prefix is strictly below D. Register\nthe needed divisor multiples in parallel. Six rounds and the response\ncycle bring down the remaining seven digits. Trial 1 needs 32 data bits,\ntrials 2 and 3 need 27 each, and trials 4 through 7 need 21 each. Use a\nseparate borrow bit and mask trials outside the active radix. This leaves\n170 trial data bits and seven residual inputs. Fixed shifts selected in\nsetup can pack the dividend groups into three-bit slots for the recurrence.\n\nCapture the small- and large-divisor completion terms at the EX/MEM edge\non response transfer. Select the architectural result and restore its sign\nin MEM for the existing WB-only dependency. Keep division off the ordinary\nEX-to-EX result bus. Preserve the standalone ALU response throughout\nbackpressure, reset cancellation, original RVFI operands and ALTOPS timing.\nA median 88.5 MHz at the champion's marker count would give 281.8 iter/s.\nThe main timing risk is the verified-load path once division leaves EX.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
