rve collision suppression, reset\ninvalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store invalidation.\nKeep the WB-only multiply interlock.\n\nA single-bank control prototype passed the canonical UART and five CRC checks\nin 3,125,942 marker cycles, saving 81,075 cycles over the champion.\nGowin measured 62.721, 65.795 and 65.795 MHz. The median gives\n210.48 iterations/s, a 2.2% gain. At that cycle count the tournament\nrequires more than 67.334 MHz. The lo\n…[5506 of 8578 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:94437c5744bc048e]…\nt committing at the RAM\nport. This covers both a newly stale row and device-specific read-during-write\nbehavior. Use the existing miss, bus and dependent-replay paths on a conflict.\nRetain the candidate across holds. Reset clears occupancy and discards pending\nwork. Keep full tag and format verification, MMIO exclusion and store handshakes.\n\nThe prediction is that registering the write address, data and enables will\nimprove median Gowin Fmax with few extra marker cycles from collision misses.\nMeasure both against 88.718 MHz and 3,140,795 cycles. At the same cycle count\nthe 4.6% replacement gate requires a median above 92.80 MHz.\n\nThe champion's reported placement-0 path runs from EX/MEM effective_addr[14]\nto the load predictor's words RAM in 17.561 ns. Round 12 also exposed a path\nfrom subword verification to this write port. The predictor currently verifies\na hit, decides whether to refresh the row and drives the RAM in one cycle.\nA branch-direction improvement in round 13 saved only 0.78% of timed cycles.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
