ming,\n  compare the captured, EX/MEM, WB and speculative-load operand candidates\n  to the saved return word in parallel and select their one-bit comparison\n  with the existing rs1 bypass enables. This keeps the 32-bit operand mux\n  and general JALR adder out of the return comparison. Bit zero is discarded\n  by JALR. A set bit one takes the existing misalignment trap and recovers to\n  PC+4. An aligned mismatch redirects to the actual forwarded x1 with bit zero\n  cleared, even though both prediction and resolution say taken. A load replay\n  or older memory stall suppresses correction and stack updates until release.\n\n  A scratch four-entry stack with comparison after forwarding took 3,128,081\n  cycles for ten iterations with both buses stalled and all five CRCs correct.\n  This saves 12,714 cycles versus the champion. At that count, acceptance\n  requires more than 92.42 MHz median. The timing hypothesis is that separating\n  the return PC register and moving comparison ahead of forwarding can reach\n  that clock. The cycle saving alone is insufficient.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Add the four-entry return stack, successor return flag and registered return PC selection. Use the selected instruction's hint and preserve redirect, hold and invalidation priority.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the issued return prediction bit and 18-bit target word in IF/ID and ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture and hold return metadata with its instruction through stalls and replay.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Validate the return against the selected forwarding source, recover a wrong target or misalignment, and emit one qualified push or pop per advancing transfer.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the resolved stack action and architectural link address between EX and IF.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    descri