{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_109", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r6s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261123-003-r6s2\ntitle: Predict formatted load results with a carry-free row lookup\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion retires 544,852 loads in 3,463,993 timed cycles. Loads can\n  wait on dmemReady and their immediate consumers wait for WB. A prediction\n  of the formatted register value can serve both the load and its consumer\n  if MEM verifies the address, access type and freshness of the prediction.\n  Recording the sign- or zero-extended value when training removes subword\n  extraction from the predictor RAM output to the consumer's EX operand.\n\n  A scratch RTL prototype completed ten CoreMark iterations in 3,187,942\n  bracketed cycles with both stall generators active and all five CRCs\n  correct. Gowin measured 58.949, 60.274 and 60.274 MHz. The median gives\n  189.07 iterations/s, 9.05% above 173.38. At this cycle count the\n  acceptance threshold requires more than 57.815 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Issue the instruction following a load under the prediction that its\n  operand will be available on the EX/MEM bypass. While EX computes the\n  load's exact address from forwarded rs1 and the signed immediate, predict\n  a row in a 256-entry load-result table. Independently add operand bits\n  [9:5] modulo 32 and [4:2] modulo 8 and concatenate the sums. Read that\n  row synchronously at the EX/MEM edge. In the prototype these short adds\n  selected the exact word index for 526,591 of the 544,852 timed loads.\n\n  Each row records the RAM address tag [19:10], byte offset, access width,\n  signedness for subword loads, the formatted 32-bit result, and the raw\n  word for RVFI. Keep one resettable validity bit per row. Capture the\n  predicted index, row and validity with the load. In MEM verify that the\n  reconstructed word address equals the full resolved word address, that\n  the access is aligned and inside ordinary RAM, and that offset and format\n  match. On a hit suppress dmemREn, complete even if dmemReady is low, and\n  bypass the stored result directly to EX. Run verification in parallel\n  with the consum\n…[1665 of 4737 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c6c7721c61fdaaf7]…\nem_stage.sv\n    description: Read the 256-row block RAM, verify the captured address and format, and provide its preformatted result to forwarding and WB. Train on read misses and accepted stores, handle collisions and retain the original word for RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Replace the blanket load-use interlock with speculative issue and a dependent-miss hold. Route verified completion, speculative EX/MEM forwarding, WB capture and replay control through the current interlocks.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: On the extra consumer hold, capture a matching older WB operand before the load takes its WB slot. Preserve the consumer PC, controls and sources for its retry.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Assert a two-cycle gap for the cold dependent load and one for each warm hit in the existing successor-replay test. Retain the exact multiply-use gaps. Cover wrong-row carries, width and sign changes, delayed partial stores, MMIO and a held dependent control transfer.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
