{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep6/formal/riscv-formal/checks/rvfi_liveness_check.sv && rg -n 'latency|liveness|10 cycles|rounds' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-170 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"// Copyright (C) 2017  Claire Xenia Wolf <claire@yosyshq.com>\n//\n// Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any\n// purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above\n// copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.\n//\n// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES\n// WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF\n// MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR\n// ANY SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES\n// WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN\n// ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF\n// OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.\n\nmodule rvfi_liveness_check (\n\tinput clock, reset, trig, check,\n\t`RVFI_INPUTS\n);\n\t`rvformal_rand_const_reg [63:0] insn_order;\n\treg found_next_insn = 0;\n\n\tinteger channel_idx;\n\talways @(posedge clock) begin\n\t\tif (reset) begin\n\t\t\tfound_next_insn = 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\tfor (channel_idx = 0; channel_idx < `RISCV_FORMAL_NRET; channel_idx=channel_idx+1) begin\n\t\t\t\tif (rvfi_valid[channel_idx] && rvfi_order[64*channel_idx +: 64] == insn_order+1) begin\n\t\t\t\t\tfound_next_insn = 1;\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (trig) begin\n\t\t\t\tassume(rvfi_valid[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(!rvfi_halt[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(insn_order == rvfi_order[64*`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX +: 64]);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (check) begin\n\t\t\t\tassert(found_next_insn);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\nendmodule\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Fold DIV and REM into four eight-bit quotient steps\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"At 5.442 MHz the baseline scores\n3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Fold DIV and REM into a four-round execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cel\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten the divider feedback path to five quotient bits per clock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's wor\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Shorten the divider feedback path with parallel radix-4 digit selection\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Gowin trace\n15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261123-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Replay short loops from a 64-word instruction buffer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion spends 4,238,604\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nlines=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor x in [lines[4],lines[5]]:\n print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],x['error'])\nPY\nls cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nlines=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor x in [lines[4],lines[5]]:\n print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],x['error'])\nPY\nls cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\"","aggregated_output":"Run the existing restoring divider for seven rounds of five quotient bits.\nLoad a 35-bit shift register with three leading zeros and the 32-bit\ndividend magnitude. Each round consumes five bits from the top, appends\nfive quotient bits at the bottom and registers the partial remainder.\nAfter 35 steps the low 32 quotient bits and the remainder give the RV32M\nresults. This cuts the chain of subtract-and-select decisions from eight\nto five while retaining the divider's current request and response ports.\n\nA scratch implementation reached 42.537, 43.681 and 43.681 MHz across\nthe three Gowin placement options. The worst paths now end at the ID/EX\noperand registers. Stalled CoreMark passed CRC validation and used\n4,491,485 marker cycles for ten iterations, matching the champion.\nThe 43.681 MHz median therefore gives 97.25 iterations/s, up 37.1%\nfrom 70.94. The three extra clocks apply to each DIV/REM on workloads\nthat use these instructions.\n None\nReplace the binary restoring round with three radix-4 digit selections per\nclock. For each digit, bring down two dividend bits and subtract D, 2D and 3D\nin parallel. The borrow bits select the largest multiple that fits, its\nresidual and the corresponding two quotient bits. Precompute the multiples\nin a setup clock so their generation is outside the recurrence. Six identical\nrounds consume a 36-bit dividend seeded with four leading zeros and yield\nthe architectural quotient in the low 32 bits. This reduces the serial\nsubtract/select depth from eight to three at the cost of two more parallel\nsubtractors per digit and three additional clocks per division.\n\nAt the champion's marker cycle count, 41.4 MHz would yield about 92.2\niterations/s, a 30% gain. The acceptance threshold is about 33.33 MHz at\nthat cycle count. Check the post-route median and marker cycles separately.\nRouting the parallel trials or the existing single-cycle multiply could\nset the new clock limit.\n None\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The champion spent 54,467 marker cycles correcting conditional branches, so even perfect direction prediction would fall short of the 4.6% margin on its own. I’m targeting the divider’s measured critical path with a prediction that the upper eight quotient bits are zero. A single magnitude comparison can validate that prediction exactly."}}
