{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'd=\"$TMPDIR/pred7.BRrZxM\"\ncat > \"$d/genvalid.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys,shutil\np=Path(sys.argv[1]);shutil.copytree(p.parent/sys.argv[2],p);f=p/'mem_stage.sv';s=f.read_text()\ns=s.replace('logic [255:0] occupied;', '''logic [15:0] group_valid;\n  (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) logic [15:0] row_valid[0:15];''')\ns=s.replace('  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\\\\n    if (reset) begin\\\\n      occupied <= \\\\'0;', '''  logic [15:0] write_mask, old_mask;\n  assign write_mask = 16'b1 << update_index[3:0];\n  assign old_mask = group_valid[update_index[7:4]] ? row_valid[update_index[7:4]] : '0;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) if (update) begin\n    row_valid[update_index[7:4]] <= install ? old_mask | write_mask : old_mask & ~write_mask;\n  end\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      group_valid <= '0;''')\ns=s.replace('if (update) occupied[update_index] <= install;', \\\"if (update) group_valid[update_index[7:4]] <= 1'b1;\\\")\ns=s.replace('occupied[lookup_index] &&', 'group_valid[lookup_index[7:4]] && row_valid[lookup_index[7:4]][lookup_index[3:0]] &&')\nf.write_text(s)\nPY\npython \\\"\"'$d/genvalid.py\" \"$d/grouped\" common\nPYTHONPATH=. python \"$d/test_timing.py\" \"$d/grouped\" \"$d/timinggrouped\" > \"$d/metricgrouped\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_90", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r7s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261123-003-r7s2\ntitle: \\\"Predict the formatted load value in EX and forward it through the ordinary result register\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion still interlocks every immediate consumer of LB, LBU, LH\n  and LHU. Its ten-iteration CoreMark bracket contained 83,985 subword\n  load-use holds with ID free to advance. The load's width, sign mode\n  and byte lane are already available in EX. Preparing the value there\n  lets a dependent instruction use the same registered operand path as\n  an integer addition.\nhypothesis: |\n  Read a 256-row distributed RAM combinationally during the producing\n  load's EX cycle. Predict the word index using the champion's two\n  independent sums of base and displacement bits [9:5] and [4:2].\n  In parallel, add the low two bits exactly to select the byte lane.\n  Use one-hot lane and width selects to form the sign- or zero-extended\n  value for LB, LBU, LH, LHU or LW. Capture that candidate directly in\n  EX/MEM.alu_result. Each consumer can now select the youngest EX/MEM\n  writer through a single data path. Keep a separate load-dependency\n  bit solely to trigger replay if MEM rejects the prediction.\n\n  Register the raw word, tag, predicted index and collision-qualified\n  occupancy with the producer. At MEM verify alignment and the entire\n  RAM word address, including the zero upper bits. On a verified hit,\n  use the registered prediction for WB and the raw word for RVFI.\n  A miss uses the actual bus word, exact lane and architectural format.\n  Hold a dependent consumer through backpressure, bubble it once on\n  completion, and retry from WB. Gate redirect, training, division and\n  writes on successful advance. Preserve collision suppression, reset\n  invalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store invalidation.\n  Keep the WB-only multiply interlock.\n\n  A scratch prototype passed the canonical UART and five CRC checks\n  in 3,125,942 marker cycles, saving 81,075 cycles over the champion.\n  Gowin measured 62.721, 65.795 and 65.795 MHz. The median gives\n  210.48 iterations/s, a 2.2% gain. At that cycle count the tournament\n  requires more than 67.334 MHz. The longest median-placement path\n  ended at the shared EX/MEM result register through the predictor read\n  and format logic. Its timing is the remaining implementation risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Generate the predictive row and exact lane and width selects in parallel. Capture the formatted load candidate in the same EX/MEM register as integer results.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Use an asynchronous distributed-RAM candidate read for EX, register its verification metadata and raw word, and select the verified candidate or formatted bus response into a common WB result.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: Select EX/MEM for every matching effective writer and retain a separate bit identifying an operand supplied by a load.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect the EX lookup and formatted prediction, reserve the proactive interlock for multiply, and use the dependent-load bit and the MEM verdict to replay rejected consumers.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: Forward and write back the completed result selected at the MEM/WB edge.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Require adjacent retirements for a warm subword load and its consumer. Check all legal lanes, sign boundaries, raw RVFI words and masks, and a dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema,pathlib,yaml\np=pathlib.Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r7s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(d['id'], 'schema valid')\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
