{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_96", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,jsonschema,json\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261123-003-r7s2.yaml')\ns=p.read_text().replace('Predict the formatted load value in EX and forward it through the ordinary result register','Predict formatted load values with four parallel banks and a registered bank select')\na=s.index('  Read a 256-row');b=s.index('  Register the raw word',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''  Split a 256-word load-value predictor into four 64-row distributed\n  RAM banks. As in the champion, assemble the predicted word index from\n  independent sums of base and displacement bits [9:5] and [4:2].\n  Use index[5:0] to read all four banks in the producer's EX cycle.\n  Add the low two address bits exactly. Format each candidate in parallel\n  for the producer's width, lane and sign mode. At EX/MEM capture the four\n  value candidates, a one-hot selection for index[7:6], and the ordinary\n  integer result separately. This moves the last two bits of row selection\n  across the register and removes the ALU-versus-load mux from the\n  predictor read path.\n\n  At each consuming EX source, qualify the four bank enables with the\n  youngest-writer load-forwarding enable. OR the masked bank outputs\n  directly with the masked captured, WB and ordinary EX/MEM operands.\n  Thus choosing the bank and choosing the bypass source need only one\n  data selection network. MEM can select the same bank in parallel for WB.\n  Full SWs and accepted read fills update just the addressed bank.\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('Register the raw word, tag, predicted index and collision-qualified','Register the matching raw word, tag, predicted index and collision-qualified')\ns=s.replace('  A scratch prototype passed','  A single-bank control prototype passed').replace('  and format logic. Its timing is the remaining implementation risk.','''  and format logic. The proposed four-bank layout targets 68.25 MHz,\n  which would give 218.33 iterations/s at the measured cycle count.\n  Its post-route clock and the delay of the consumer mux remain unmeasured.''')\ns=s.replace('fitness_delta_pct: 2','fitness_delta_pct: 6').replace('confidence: medium','confidence: low')\ns=s.replace('Generate the predictive row and exact lane and width selects in parallel. Capture the formatted load candidate in the same EX/MEM register as integer results.','Capture the four formatted load candidates and one-hot bank choice beside the producer. Merge bank and bypass selection for each consumer, preserving hold and replay behavior.')\ns=s.replace('Use an asynchronous distributed-RAM candidate read for EX, register its verification metadata and raw word, and select the verified candidate or formatted bus response into a common WB result.','Partition the data by the upper two index bits. Read four 64-row banks in parallel, format each candidate, verify the selected row and send the accepted value or formatted bus response to WB.')\ns=s.replace('Select EX/MEM for every matching effective writer and retain a separate bit identifying an operand supplied by a load.','Use the registered bank choice and youngest-writer load match to generate bank-specific operand enables. Keep the combined load match for replay.')\ns=s.replace('the EX lookup and formatted prediction','the EX lookup, four predictions and registered bank select')\ns=s.replace('Check all legal lanes, sign boundaries, raw RVFI words and masks, and a dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.','Check all four banks at the same row offset with different words, every legal lane and sign boundary, raw RVFI words and masks, and a dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.')\ns=s.replace('The proposed four-bank layout','All 30 directed pipeline cases passed on the control prototype. The proposed four-bank layout')\ndoc=yaml.safe_load(s);jsonsch