{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id'].endswith(('r5s2','r6s2','r7s0','r7s2')):\n  print(x['id'],x['hypothesis'])\n  print(x['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-003-r5s2 {'motivation': \"The champion needs 4,238,604 cycles for ten timed CoreMark iterations.\\nAn earlier predecessor-indexed instruction predictor saved 17.8% of cycles\\non the prior core, including over 68,000 issues at nonsequential successors\\nwhile imemReady was low. That experiment preceded the move of multiplication\\ninto MEM. The opportunity on the 61.962 MHz champion is to recover those\\nfetch slots while keeping the predictor's RAM output off the target adder.\\n\\nA scratch prototype on the current champion took 3,463,993 bracketed cycles\\nwith both stall generators active, an 18.3% reduction. All five CRCs\\nmatched. During the timing bracket, 604,761 instructions issued from\\nverified predictions with imemReady low, including 69,294 at nonsequential\\nsuccessors. Fetch selected the precomputed direct target on 74,650 of\\nthose issues.\\n\\nGowin reported 57.937, 60.148 and 60.148 MHz. The median gives 173.64\\niterations/s, 18.8% above 146.18. At this cycle count the 4.6% acceptance\\nmargin requires 52.966 MHz. Placement zero used 4,120 logic cells, 1,177\\nregisters and eight block RAMs. The prototype passed all 53 single-retire\\nALTOPS formal checks and 21 pipeline cases. Its retirement trace matched\\nthe ISS on selftest and all three random programs with both stalls enabled.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"On each accepted fetch, use the current PC[10:2] to read a 512-entry\\nsynchronous last-successor table. Each row carries the observed successor's\\n18-bit word address, its 32-bit instruction, its 18-bit direct target word\\naddress and two flags for a legal, aligned, in-range JAL or conditional\\nbranch. Compute the flags and target from the live instruction and its PC\\nwhen filling the row. The 70-bit payload fits two 36-bit-wide block RAM\\nbanks at depth 512. Keep one resettable occupancy bit per row.\\n\\nOn a ready bus, issue the live word and use its direct-target calculation.\\nDuring an imem stall, issue the registered candidate only if occupied and\\nits reconstructed byte address equals the entire \n…[18063 of 21135 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:153ed6add85e72d1]…\nfour 64-row banks in parallel, format each candidate, verify the selected row and send the accepted value or formatted bus response to WB.'}, {'file': 'rtl/forward_unit.sv', 'description': 'Use the registered bank choice and youngest-writer load match to generate bank-specific operand enables. Keep the combined load match for replay.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX lookup, four predictions and registered bank select, reserve the proactive interlock for multiply, and use the dependent-load bit and the MEM verdict to replay rejected consumers.'}, {'file': 'rtl/wb_stage.sv', 'description': 'Forward and write back the completed result selected at the MEM/WB edge.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Require adjacent retirements for a warm subword load and its consumer. Check all four banks at the same row offset with different words, every legal lane and sign boundary, raw RVFI words and masks, and a dependent branch after a conflicting narrow store with dmem stalled.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
