{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '207,270p' tools/eval/fpga.py && sed -n '70,180p' test/cosim/main.cpp\"", "aggregated_output": "    worktree_path = Path(worktree).resolve()\n    if sim_bin is None:\n        sim_bin = str(worktree_path / \"test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim\")\n    elf     = str(worktree_path / \"bench/programs/coremark.elf\")\n    # 50M cycle ceiling: 2K CoreMark with ITERATIONS=10 + iStall+dStall\n    # needs ~5M cycles. 50M gives 10x headroom for slower candidates.\n    try:\n        result = run_pgroup(\n            [sim_bin, elf, \"50000000\"] + COREMARK_SIM_FLAGS,\n            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=600, env=env\n        )\n    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:\n        return {'completed': False, 'iter_per_cycle': 0.0, 'cycles': 0, 'iterations': 0,\n                'reason': f'coremark_harness_error: {e}'}\n    lines = [l for l in result.stdout.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    if len(lines) < 2:\n        return {'completed': False, 'iter_per_cycle': 0.0, 'cycles': 0, 'iterations': 0,\n                'reason': 'no output from sim'}\n\n    # Last line is the ebreak/maxcycles marker; second-to-last is the final retirement.\n    try:\n        marker = json.loads(lines[-1])\n        last_retirement = json.loads(lines[-2])\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        return {'completed': False, 'iter_per_cycle': 0.0, 'cycles': 0, 'iterations': 0,\n                'reason': f'malformed sim output: {e}'}\n\n    if not marker.get('ebreak', False):\n        # Benchmark ran out of cycles before finishing. Score 0 — don't credit\n        # a hung CPU with whatever cycle count it happened to reach.\n        return {'completed': False, 'iter_per_cycle': 0.0, 'cycles': 0, 'iterations': 0,\n                'reason': 'maxcycles_hit_before_ebreak'}\n\n    # OOB sticky flag from the sim: if the CPU addressed outside 1 MiB at any\n    # point during this run, the cycle count we're about to divide by is tainted\n    # by silently-wrapped memory accesses. Treat as a benchmark failure — the\n    # same rule cosim applies, so a CPU that produces a correct CRC via aliased\n    # memory doesn't earn a fitness score.\n    if marker.get('oob', False):\n     \n…[6262 of 9334 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dfbbe83f02f9b03c]…\n        } else if (addr == BENCH_STOP_ADDR) {\n                // Last stop_time() call wins — CoreMark calls it once, but\n                // tolerate multiple if a bench program re-times.\n                bench_stop_cycle = cycle; bench_stop_set = true;\n            } else if (in_uart_range(addr)) {\n                for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n                    if ((top->io_dmemWEn >> i) & 1) {\n                        char c = (top->io_dmemWData >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF;\n                        if (c) uart_buf.push_back(c);\n                    }\n                }\n            } else if (in_mem_range(addr)) {\n                ww(dmem, addr, top->io_dmemWData, top->io_dmemWEn);\n            } else {\n                // OOB write (neither dmem nor UART). Flag so testbench reports it.\n                oob_access = true;\n            }\n        }\n\n        top->clock = 1; top->eval();\n\n        // Drain channel 0 then channel 1 (NRET=2 contract). For V0\n        // single-issue, channel 1's valid is always 0, so the JSON stream\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(l)\n if x['id'].endswith(('r6s1','r6s2','r7s2')):\n  h=x['hypothesis'];print(x['id']);print(h['motivation'] if isinstance(h,dict) else '');print(h['hypothesis'][:3500] if isinstance(h,dict) else h[:3000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(l)\n if x['id'].endswith(('r6s1','r6s2','r7s2')):\n  h=x['hypothesis'];print(x['id']);print(h['motivation'] if isinstance(h,dict) else '');print(h['hypothesis'][:3500] if isinstance(h,dict) else h[:3000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261123-002-r6s1\nThe champion takes 3,463,993 marker cycles for ten iterations at 60.060 MHz.\nIts reported 23.186 ns path runs from the register file through EX to data RAM.\nRegister-file write-through, forwarding priority and ALU operand selection\ncan all contribute mux delay. Decode already knows the incoming source\nindices and the destinations of all three older in-flight instructions.\n\nMove forwarding arbitration across the ID/EX register. For each source, decode\nselects the youngest effective writer and registers a one-hot mask that names\nwhere its value will be in the following cycle. EX forms each operand by ORing\nthe masked data buses. Give raw word-load data its own input so an aligned LW\nand its immediate consumer can advance on successive clocks. Give the ALU\ninputs their own registered masks with PC and immediate choices so those muxes\nalso resolve in decode. Byte and halfword loads and multiplies use the existing\nWB interlock.\n\nA scratch prototype on this champion completed ten iterations in 3,344,675\nmarker cycles with all five CRCs correct. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2\nreached 63.152, 65.278 and 65.278 MHz. The median gives 195.17 iterations/s,\n12.57 percent above the champion. The prototype passed all 53 fast formal checks.\n\nhyp-20261123-003-r6s2\nThe champion executes 544,852 loads in 3,463,993 timed CoreMark cycles.\nToday an instruction that consumes an LW waits one cycle even when that\nword was just loaded or stored. Predicting the word from a partial\naddress lets the consumer start EX while MEM verifies the prediction.\nAn unshifted LW result fits directly on the forwarding path.\n\nA scratch RTL prototype selected the exact word index on 526,591 loads\nand verified 502,777 words, including 110,102 while dmemReady was low.\nOnly 3,081 completed misses required a dependent instruction to retry.\nIt completed ten iterations in 3,207,017 bracketed cycles with both\nstall generators active, all five CRCs correct and validated UART output.\nGowin measured 59.060, 63.591 and 63.591 MHz. The median\n…[4649 of 7721 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:621a27b5724f4198]…\ne and architectural format.\nHold a dependent consumer through backpressure, bubble it once on\ncompletion, and retry from WB. Gate redirect, training, division and\nwrites on successful advance. Preserve collision suppression, reset\ninvalidation, accepted SW installation and narrow-store invalidation.\nKeep the WB-only multiply interlock.\n\nA single-bank control prototype passed the canonical UART and five CRC checks\nin 3,125,942 marker cycles, saving 81,075 cycles over the champion.\nGowin measured 62.721, 65.795 and 65.795 MHz. The median gives\n210.48 iterations/s, a 2.2% gain. At that cycle count the tournament\nrequires more than 67.334 MHz. The longest median-placement path\nended at the shared EX/MEM result register through the predictor read\nand format logic. All 30 directed pipeline cases passed on the control prototype. The proposed four-bank layout targets 68.25 MHz,\nwhich would give 218.33 iterations/s at the measured cycle count.\nIts post-route clock and the delay of the consumer mux remain unmeasured.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
